{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778878027461,"sessionID":"ses_1d29c3b77ffe0TXS8qv1lJEp7L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_NCz6BVIhHXkGfTtb8eLtl1Tt","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"source-use|use_rs|uses_rs|operand-use|live-source|rs1/use|rs2/use","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"log.jsonl"},"output":"Found 2 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Gate dead forwarding compares\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Thread the decoded control bundle into the forwarding logic and short-circuit\\nequality compares for source operands the instruction cannot actually use.\\nInstructions like OP-IMM, loads, JAL, LUI, and AUIPC should skip the dead\\ncompare path entirely while preserving the existing forwarding priority when\\na source is live. This should trim the common EX cone without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 327.95, \"delta_pct\": -2.31...\n  Line 26: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r9s0\", \"title\": \"Source-use mask\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends much of its time on op-imm, loads, and simple control\\nflow, yet the core still evaluates both forwarding compare trees and the\\nload-use hazard compare on every cycle. On a small FPGA, those dead\\nequality chains and their fanout are a plausible Fmax limiter even when\\nthe ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends much of its time on op-imm, loads, and simple control\\nflow, yet the core still evaluates both forwarding compare trees and the\\nload-use hazard compare on every cycle. On a small FPGA, those dead\\nequality chains and their fanout are a plausible Fmax limiter even when\\nthe ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add compact source-operand-use flags to the decoded control bundle and use\\nthem to gate only the compare trees for operands the current instruction\\ncannot read. That lets forwarding and load-use detection skip the rs2 path\\nfor immediate-style and other single-source instructions while preserving\\nthe existing retirement semantics, forwarding priority, and stall rules.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add compact source-use flags to the decoded control bundle so later stages can tell whether rs1 and rs2 are live.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the source-use flags for each opcode class while keeping the existing legality and control decode unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the new source-use flags into the ID/EX register alongside the existing decoded control bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the rs1/rs2 equality trees with the live-source flags so dead operands do not pay for compare work.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the same live-source flags to skip unnecessary load-use co...","metadata":{"matches":2,"truncated":false},"title":"source-use|use_rs|uses_rs|operand-use|live-source|rs1/use|rs2/use","time":{"start":1778878027443,"end":1778878027460}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_00e18f6dfff683ad016a07864b5124819b98a43818a50d8996"}},"id":"prt_e2d6496b00016EORYjXS0fqkzF","sessionID":"ses_1d29c3b77ffe0TXS8qv1lJEp7L","messageID":"msg_e2d6488230019rYPFSPztIzD7b"}}
