{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778878060489,"sessionID":"ses_1d29c3b77ffe0TXS8qv1lJEp7L","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_S4SoyTijsqes5HcUEXbxOWG1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r11s0\n+title: \"Drop regfile write-through\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The regfile currently pays for same-cycle write-first bypass on both read\n+  ports, even though the EX-stage forwarding network already resolves the real\n+  RAW hazards. Removing that always-on compare/mux work should shorten the ID\n+  cone a little and may help Fmax on the Tang Nano 20K.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Make the register file a plain synchronous-write, combinational-read block\n+  with no same-cycle write-through bypass on its read ports. The pipeline\n+  already forwards newer values in EX, so this should preserve architectural\n+  behavior while trimming redundant compare/mux logic from the hot decode path.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 3\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n+    description: \"Remove the same-cycle write-first bypass from both read ports so the regfile read cone is simpler and the existing EX forwarding path handles freshness.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r11