{"type":"text","timestamp":1778879110855,"sessionID":"ses_1d28b920bffe6Yk5cv2V8sbKtD","part":{"id":"prt_e2d751db300100x1840tLS17n2","messageID":"msg_e2d74de9f001J2R15yxMunugcs","sessionID":"ses_1d28b920bffe6Yk5cv2V8sbKtD","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis file now. It will stay within `cores/bench/rtl/` changes and keep the contract untouched.","time":{"start":1778879110579,"end":1778879110854},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_09c149c061a6ed01016a078a8675208191a909d751e1b2e7ae","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778879114393,"sessionID":"ses_1d28b920bffe6Yk5cv2V8sbKtD","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_4ik4aykqWBWZgv84CfiY6D8W","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Live-source compare gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends much of its time on instructions that do not read both\n+  source operands, yet the forwarding and load-use logic still evaluates the\n+  full rs1/rs2 compare trees every cycle. On a small FPGA, that dead equality\n+  work is a plausible Fmax limiter.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add compact source-use flags to the decoded control bundle and use them to\n+  gate only the compare trees for operands the current instruction cannot\n+  read. Instructions like OP-IMM, loads, JAL, LUI, and AUIPC should skip the\n+  dead rs2 path entirely while preserving the existing forwarding priority\n+  and load-use stall rules. This should trim the common ID/EX cone without\n+  changing architectural behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact source-use flags to the control bundle so later stages can tell whether rs1 and rs2 are live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the source-use flags for each opcode class while keeping the existing legality and control decode unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the new source-use flags into the ID/EX register alongside the existing decoded control bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the rs1/rs2 equality trees with the live-source flags so dead operands do not pay for compare work.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the same live-source flags to skip unnecessary load-use comparisons for operands the instruction cannot actually read.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r12s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r12s0\n+title: \"Live-source compare gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends much of its time on instructions that do not read both\n+  source operands, yet the forwarding and load-use logic still evaluates the\n+  full rs1/rs2 compare trees every cycle. On a small FPGA, that dead equality\n+  work is a plausible Fmax limiter.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add compact source-use flags to the decoded control bundle and use them to\n+  gate only the compare trees for operands the current instruction cannot\n+  read. Instructions like OP-IMM, loads, JAL, LUI, and AUIPC should skip the\n+  dead rs2 path entirely while preserving the existing forwarding priority\n+  and load-use stall rules. This should trim the common ID/EX cone without\n+  changing architectural behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact source-use flags to the control bundle so later stages can tell whether rs1 and rs2 are live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the source-use flags for each opcode class while keeping the existing legality and control decode unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Thread