{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1778884156770,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8f15ffehkUuPe0PG0dScm","part":{"id":"prt_e2dc21d6000190lczhC2LV1Xny","messageID":"msg_e2dc218b10010vJqxo03dviNSN","sessionID":"ses_1d23e8f15ffehkUuPe0PG0dScm","snapshot":"2e7a3e6d778f0e1294d2420335e430bb2b430600","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1778884171279,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8f15ffehkUuPe0PG0dScm","part":{"id":"prt_e2dc2560b001475iURkvPwm2pG","messageID":"msg_e2dc218b10010vJqxo03dviNSN","sessionID":"ses_1d23e8f15ffehkUuPe0PG0dScm","type":"text","text":"The most promising new angle is the multiplier cone: `alu.sv` currently computes all three 64-bit products on every cycle even when the instruction is not an M-op. I’m writing a narrow hypothesis that moves that work behind the M-extension arm so the common path stays lighter.","time":{"start":1778884171275,"end":1778884171278},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_03115d554e48e29b016a079e4b0df08199af750e32e451aea7","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778884172051,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8f15ffehkUuPe0PG0dScm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_o7IIiJPA5WmCVfOqY9qCaYWS","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\n+title: \"Gate always-on multiplier work\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends most cycles on non-M instructions, but the current ALU still\n+  computes three 64-bit products on every cycle before the opcode case selects\n+  a result. That keeps multiplier fanout in the common execute cone even when\n+  the instruction is just ADD, LOAD, BRANCH, or a shift.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move the 64-bit product generation behind the M-extension arm so the common\n+  non-M path does not pay for always-on multiply logic. Keep the ALTOPS branch\n+  and the real RV32M branch behaviorally identical, but let synthesis see a\n+  smaller fast path for the instructions CoreMark executes most often.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the signed and unsigned 64-bit products only when an M-extension opcode is selected, while preserving the existing ALTOPS and real-arithmetic results.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\n+title: \"Gate always-on multiplier work\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends most cycles on non-M instructions, but the current ALU still\n+  computes three 64-bit products on every cycle before the opcode case selects\n+  a result. That keeps multiplier fanout in the common execute cone even when\n+  the instruction is just ADD, LOAD, BRANCH, or a shift.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move the 64-bit product generation behind the M-extension arm so the common\n+  non-M path does not pay for always-on multiply logic. Keep the ALTOPS branch\n+  and the real RV32M branch behaviorally identical, but let synthesis see a\n+  smaller fast path for the instructions CoreMark executes most often.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the signed and unsigned 64-bit products only when an M-extension opcode is selected, while preserving the existing ALTOPS and real-arithmetic results.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\n+title: \"Gate always-on multiplier work\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends most cycles on non-M instructions, but the current ALU still\n+  computes three 64-bit products on every cycle before the opcode case selects\n+  a result. That keeps multiplier fanout in the common execute cone even when\n+  the instruction is just ADD, LOAD, BRANCH, or a shift.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move the 64-bit product generation behind the M-extension arm so the common\n+  non-M path does not pay for always-on multiply logic. Keep the ALTOPS branch\n+  and the real RV32M branch behaviorally identical, but let synthesis see a\n+  smaller fast path for the instructions CoreMark executes most often.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Compute the signed and unsigned 64-bit products only when an M-extension opcode is selected, while preserving the existing ALTOPS and real-arithmetic results.\"\n","additions":19,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778884172036,"end":1778884172049}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03115d554e48e29b016a079e4b2e0c8199b1efecf0134ab681"}},"id":"prt_e2dc2560e004BiroVJ0Irw1vBL","sessionID":"ses_1d23e8f15ffehkUuPe0PG0dScm","messageID":"msg_e2dc218b10010vJqxo03dviNSN"}}
