"Resolve conditional branch compare and misalignment checks in decode, then emit the early redirect information.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove branch compare work from the hot EX cone and keep JALR plus non-branch ALU work on the live execute path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect control so the ID-stage branch resolver can drive fetch without waiting for EX on B-type branches.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retarget operand selection so ID can see fresher rs1/rs2 values for conditional branch compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"descri...\n  Line 17: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r6s0\", \"title\": \"Retimed memory lane metadata\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The MEM stage still recomputes byte masks, alignment, and load extraction\\nfrom the full ALU result on every load/store. On a small FPGA, that keeps\\na fairly wide combinational cone on the memory side of the pipe.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The MEM stage still recomputes byte masks, alignment, and load extraction\\nfrom the full ALU result on every load/store. On a small FPGA, that keeps\\na fairly wide combinational cone on the memory side of the pipe.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute the load/store lane metadata in EX and carry it through the\\nEX/MEM payload so MEM only performs the actual bus access plus a much\\nsmaller extract/extend step. This should trim the common memory-path logic\\nwithout changing retirement semantics or ISA-visible behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM sideband fields for predecoded lane metadata such as alignment, mask, and shift information.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the memory lane metadata once the effective address is known, instead of re-deriving it in MEM.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried metadata so byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic no longer dominate the MEM cone.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM sideband fields for predecoded lane metadata such as alignment, mask, and shift information.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the memory lane metadata once the effective address is known, instead of re-deriving it in MEM.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried metadata so byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic no longer dominate the MEM cone.\"}], \"outcome\": \"i...\n  Line 20: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Reuse JALR sum\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\\nadder even though the main ALU already produces the same sum for JALR\\ninstructions. That duplicate arithmetic sits in the hot execute cone and\\ncan be shaved without changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\\nadder even though the main ALU already produces the same sum for JALR\\ninstructions. That duplicate arithmetic sits in the hot execute cone and\\ncan be shaved without changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Reuse the main ALU result for JALR redirect generation and factor the\\nrepeated `pc + 4` expression into a shared local so EX does not carry a\\nsecond 32-bit adder for the same instruction. This should trim a small\\namount of combinational depth from the common execute path while keeping\\nthe architectural JAL/JALR results unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\