{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778889273743,"sessionID":"ses_1d1f07bb8ffeyZ28McrXzyNs16","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_3BA7ZZnvF2RJ6uSpn43RygKL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r15s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r15s0\n+title: \"Local source-use gating\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The forwarding and load-use logic still evaluates compare trees for source\n+  operands the current instruction cannot actually read. That dead equality\n+  work sits on the hot decode/execute boundary and is a plausible Fmax drag on\n+  Tang Nano 20K.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Derive exact source-liveness locally from the existing decoded control bits\n+  and use it to short-circuit the unused rs2 compare path in forwarding and\n+  hazard detection. Keep the instruction semantics, stall rules, and RVFI\n+  stream unchanged, but let synthesis prune dead compare/fanout work without\n+  introducing new architectural state or fetch-side speculation.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the rs1/rs2 compare trees with locally-derived source-use conditions so dead operands do not pay for equality checks.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip the rs2 load-use compare when the decoded instruction cannot read rs2, while preserving the existing stall behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the existing decode/control view into forwarding so source-liveness can be derived without widening the architectural state.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r15s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r15s0.yaml\n========