{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778889278541,"sessionID":"ses_1d1f07bb8ffeyZ28McrXzyNs16","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_bQIaIyhhaCSxQnHV8XdIklvC","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r15s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r15s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r15s0\n2: title: \"Local source-use gating\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The forwarding and load-use logic still evaluates compare trees for source\n6:   operands the current instruction cannot actually read. That dead equality\n7:   work sits on the hot decode/execute boundary and is a plausible Fmax drag on\n8:   Tang Nano 20K.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Derive exact source-liveness locally from the existing decoded control bits\n11:   and use it to short-circuit the unused rs2 compare path in forwarding and\n12:   hazard detection. Keep the instruction semantics, stall rules, and RVFI\n13:   stream unchanged, but let synthesis prune dead compare/fanout work without\n14:   introducing new architectural state or fetch-side speculation.\n15: expected_impact:\n16:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n17:   confidence: medium\n18: changes:\n19:   - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n20:     description: \"Gate the rs1/rs2 compare trees with locally-derived source-use conditions so dead operands do not pay for equality checks.\"\n21:   - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n22:     description: \"Skip the rs2 load-use compare when the decoded instruction cannot read rs2, while preserving the existing stall behavior.\"\n23:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n24:     description: \"Thread the existing decode/control view into forwarding so source-liveness can be derived without widening the architectural state.\"\n\n(End of file - total 24 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-001-r15s0\ntitle: \"Local source-use gating\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The forwarding and load-use logic still evaluates compare trees for source\n  operands the current instruction cannot actually read. That dead equality\n  work sits on the hot decode/execute boundary and is a plausible Fmax drag on\n  Tang Nano 20K.\nhypothesis: |\n  Derive exact source-liveness locally from the existing decoded control bits\n  and use it to short-circuit the unused rs2 compare path in forwarding and\n  hazard detection. Keep the instruction semantics, stall rules, and RVFI\n  stream unchanged, but let synthesis prune dead compare/fanout work without\n  introducing new architectural state or fetch-side speculation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Gate the rs1/rs2 compare trees with locally-derived source-use conditions so dead operands do not pay for equality checks.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r15s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778889278510,"end":1778889278540}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_02eacd7d07ae5e24016a07b23e61e0819a8aef280425dacfdf"}},"id":"prt_e2e104428001cD14kVMTrm9NiN","sessionID":"ses_1d1f07bb8ffeyZ28McrXzyNs16","messageID":"msg_e2e1033cf001Y8nOdiBcIUi9uK"}}
