{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778854688648,"sessionID":"ses_1d4015996ffeYzh1mAnjgF53FR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_xeNQ85KYhiqpJ5bN2iEDrZ8T","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":100},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-003-r3s2\n2: title: \"Tiny BTB target cache\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark loops revisit the same taken branches many times, but this core\n6:   still fetches sequentially until EX resolves control flow. A tiny target\n7:   cache can turn repeated loop branches into predicted fetches and trim the\n8:   recurring wrong-path flush cost without changing architectural behavior.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer in IF that stores the\n11:   PC tag and resolved target for taken B-type branches and JALs. On a BTB\n12:   hit, fetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through as usual.\n13:   Update the entry from the existing EX redirect path so the predictor uses\n14:   cached targets instead of re-decoding branch immediates in fetch.\n15: expected_impact:\n16:   fitness_delta_pct: 6\n17:   confidence: medium\n18: changes:\n19:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n20:     description: \"Add BTB lookup/predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"\n21:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Train the BTB from resolved taken branches and JAL redirects.\"\n23:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n24:     description: \"Add any small predictor-sideband fields needed to carry BTB state cleanly.\"\n\n(End of file - total 24 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Tiny BTB target cache\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark loops revisit the same taken branches many times, but this core\n  still fetches sequentially until EX resolves control flow. A tiny target\n  cache can turn repeated loop branches into predicted fetches and trim the\n  recurring wrong-path flush cost without changing architectural behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer in IF that stores the\n  PC tag and resolved target for taken B-type branches and JALs. On a BTB\n  hit, fetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through as usual.\n  Update the entry from the existing EX redirect path so the predictor uses\n  cached targets instead of re-decoding branch immediates in fetch.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add BTB lookup/predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778854688630,"end":1778854688646}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0c4e9d0e97b58770016a072b20269c819ba435997626f28005"}},"id":"prt_e2c007774001eSGWrKVjjwo4dZ","sessionID":"ses_1d4015996ffeYzh1mAnjgF53FR","messageID":"msg_e2c006558001VFxkijIpxSUkeS"}}
