{"type":"text","timestamp":1778854724679,"sessionID":"ses_1d4015996ffeYzh1mAnjgF53FR","part":{"id":"prt_e2c010407001OX71rK01C6Cuz2","messageID":"msg_e2c00785d001x2mpb5SCa4JpUo","sessionID":"ses_1d4015996ffeYzh1mAnjgF53FR","type":"text","text":"Writing the required `r3s0` file now. I’m keeping it narrow to the EX forwarding cone so it stays a true micro-opt hypothesis.","time":{"start":1778854724615,"end":1778854724678},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_098ead99e745eac5016a072b447c98819b99defcdeb5cdc5cc","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778854725627,"sessionID":"ses_1d4015996ffeYzh1mAnjgF53FR","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_N4jgCi7Pr2qzzdf8ZgYbAvZs","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\n+title: \"Gate dead forwarding compares\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\n+  read one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\n+  rs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\n+  the EX input path on a small FPGA.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Thread the decoded control bundle into the forwarding logic and short-circuit\n+  equality compares for source operands the instruction cannot actually use.\n+  Instructions like OP-IMM, loads, JAL, LUI, and AUIPC should skip the dead\n+  compare path entirely while preserving the existing forwarding priority when\n+  a source is live. This should trim the common EX cone without changing ISA\n+  behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r3s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gp