 rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 327.95, \"delta_pct\": -2.31...\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass selection into ID, latch already-forwarded\\nrs1/rs2 values in the ID/EX register, and let EX consume stable operands\\ndirectly. Keep the existing load-use stall rule and x0 filtering intact so\\ncorrectness stays the same while the EX combinational cone gets shorter.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwarding before the ID/EX flop and latch the selected operands into the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume pre-forwarded operands directly and drop the operand-select muxes from the EX critical path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retime or simplify bypass selection so it serves the ID-side operand latch instead of EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwardin...","metadata":{"matches":2,"truncated":false},"title":"load-use|forward_unit|hazard_unit|reg_file","time":{"start":1778864243813,"end":1778864243829}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_00c2e42da0ea2009016a075073a3b48198ac9c964983543312"}},"id":"prt_e2c924453001Fw1OR233FIn98Y","sessionID":"ses_1d36e7861ffePEVs6BESHPQc43","messageID":"msg_e2c91f5750014CA27KQqO4zNM2"}}
