{"type":"text","timestamp":1778864319018,"sessionID":"ses_1d36e7861ffePEVs6BESHPQc43","part":{"id":"prt_e2c9369da001y1uN6FSJQHPSP9","messageID":"msg_e2c92d4cc001TioeSY9ua6vzji","sessionID":"ses_1d36e7861ffePEVs6BESHPQc43","type":"text","text":"I’ve settled on a single load/store-path retime: move lane metadata out of the MEM stage so the hot memory cone gets smaller without touching control-flow or forwarding behavior.","time":{"start":1778864318938,"end":1778864319017},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_06ffd74f79396c48016a0750bece48819bb5d6c8e05d5c2545","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778864320302,"sessionID":"ses_1d36e7861ffePEVs6BESHPQc43","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_GUlTi7cV8z4e1eaTfUV6S8oJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\n+title: \"Retime load/store lane metadata\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\n+  extraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\n+  loads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\n+  raise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Precompute and carry the load/store lane metadata out of EX: word-aligned\n+  address, byte mask, and byte-lane shift/selection can be latched with the\n+  EX/MEM payload so MEM only has to perform the actual memory access and a\n+  much smaller extract/extend step. This should reduce the hot memory-path\n+  logic seen by synthesis while preserving retirement semantics.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the lane metadata once the ALU result is known so the memory stage no longer needs to decode width/address details.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the carried metadata to simplify byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic on the MEM critical path.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\n+title: \"Retime load/store lane metadata\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\n+  extraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\n+  loads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\n+  raise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Precompute and carry the load/store lane metadata out of EX: word-aligned\n+  address, byte mask, and byte-lane shift/selection can be latched with the\n+  EX/MEM payload so MEM only has to perform the actual memory access and a\n+  much smaller extract/extend step. This should reduce the hot memory-path\n+  logic seen by synthesis while preserving retirement semantics.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the lane metadata once the ALU result is known so the memory stage no longer needs to decode width/address details.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the carried metadata to simplify byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic on the MEM critical path.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/exper