{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778864325427,"sessionID":"ses_1d36e7861ffePEVs6BESHPQc43","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_U3h412DZNF8H4P07R8X9DYAI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\n2: title: \"Retime load/store lane metadata\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\n6:   extraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\n7:   loads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\n8:   raise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Precompute and carry the load/store lane metadata out of EX: word-aligned\n11:   address, byte mask, and byte-lane shift/selection can be latched with the\n12:   EX/MEM payload so MEM only has to perform the actual memory access and a\n13:   much smaller extract/extend step. This should reduce the hot memory-path\n14:   logic seen by synthesis while preserving retirement semantics.\n15: expected_impact:\n16:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n17:   confidence: medium\n18: changes:\n19:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n20:     description: \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"\n21:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Populate the lane metadata once the ALU result is known so the memory stage no longer needs to decode width/address details.\"\n23:   - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n24:     description: \"Consume the carried metadata to simplify byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic on the MEM critical path.\"\n\n(End of file - total 24 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\ntitle: \"Retime load/store lane metadata\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\n  extraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\n  loads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\n  raise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\nhypothesis: |\n  Precompute and carry the load/store lane metadata out of EX: word-aligned\n  address, byte mask, and byte-lane shift/selection can be latched with the\n  EX/MEM payload so MEM only has to perform the actual memory access and a\n  much smaller extract/extend step. This should reduce the hot memory-path\n  logic seen by synthesis while preserving retirement semantics.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r4s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778864325417,"end":1778864325426}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03bf183c521911c9016a0750c54d1c819aa68cdcdf3a2b85a8"}},"id":"prt_e2c93831d001lNhbjG1SxS9yae","sessionID":"ses_1d36e7861ffePEVs6BESHPQc43","messageID":"msg_e2c936ffc001En7IQO9dQSBPXm"}}
