{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778869730107,"sessionID":"ses_1d31b6527ffeXi6zx336Z6AZaO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_3NjfgFFKyouGmEz19BKo3LXH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r5s0\n+title: \"Predecode hot instruction fields\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current decode path fans the full 32-bit instruction into legality,\n+  register address extraction, and hazard checks. On a small FPGA, that\n+  repeated slicing and nested opcode logic is a plausible Fmax limiter once\n+  the branch-target cone has already been trimmed.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move instruction-field extraction to the IF/ID boundary: latch opcode,\n+  funct3, funct7, rd, rs1, rs2, and EBREAK qualification in the pipeline\n+  bundle, then have `decoder` and `hazard_unit` consume those predecoded\n+  fields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction word. This should cut\n+  decode fanout and simplify the common ID critical path without changing\n+  ISA-visible behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add predecoded IF/ID sideband fields for opcode/funct/register-address metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Extract and latch the instruction metadata once when fetching, including EBREAK qualification.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the narrower predecoded fields instead of repeatedly slicing the raw instruction bus.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the latched source register addresses from IF/ID so load-use checks stop fanning out the full instruction word.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the new predecoded bundle through decode and keep the ID/EX register semantics unchanged.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r5s0\n+title: \"Predecode hot instruction fields\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current decode path fans the full 32-bit instruction into legality,\n+  register address extraction, and hazard checks. On a small FPGA, that\n+  repeated slicing and nested opcode logic is a plausible Fmax limiter once\n+  the branch-target cone has already been trimmed.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move instruction-field extraction to the IF/ID boundary: latch opcode,\n+  funct3, funct7, rd, rs1, rs2, and EBREAK qualification in the pipeline\n+  bundle, then have `decoder` and `hazard_unit` consume those predecoded\n+  fields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction word. This should cut\n+  decode fanout and simplify the common ID critical path without changing\n+  ISA-visible behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add predecoded IF/ID sideband fields for opcode/funct/register-address metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Extract and latch the instruction metadata once when fetching, including EBREAK qualification.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the narrower predecoded fields instead of repeatedly slicing the raw instruction bus.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the latched source register addresses from IF/ID so load-use checks stop fanning out the full instruction word.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the new predecoded bundle through decode and keep the ID/EX register semantics unchanged.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r5s0\n+title: \"Predecode hot instruction fields\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  The current decode path fans the full 32-bit instruction into legality,\n+  register address extraction, and hazard checks. On a small FPGA, that\n+  repeated slicing and nested opcode logic is a plausible Fmax limiter once\n+  the branch-target cone has already been trimmed.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move instruction-field extraction to the IF/ID boundary: latch opcode,\n+  funct3, funct7, rd, rs1, rs2, and EBREAK qualification in the pipeline\n+  bundle, then have `decoder` and `hazard_unit` consume those predecoded\n+  fields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction word. This should cut\n+  decode fanout and simplify the common ID critical path without changing\n+  ISA-visible behavior.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add predecoded IF/ID sideband fields for opcode/funct/register-address metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Extract and latch the instruction metadata once when fetching, including EBREAK qualification.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the narrower predecoded fields instead of repeatedly slicing the raw instruction bus.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the latched source register addresses from IF/ID so load-use checks stop fanning out the full instruction word.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the new predecoded bundle through decode and keep the ID/EX register semantics unchanged.\"\n","additions":29,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r5s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778869730103,"end":1778869730106}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f9d1272bf8622da016a0765e0842c819188d8009ccde9a041"}},"id":"prt_e2ce5f536001GJ5KNgupyjsUvw","sessionID":"ses_1d31b6527ffeXi6zx336Z6AZaO","messageID":"msg_e2ce5aae8001KLGrSSdGfGpjI5"}}
