{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778871568779,"sessionID":"ses_1d2fe3047ffeNwTumIICkSX4cE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_PHXTacJBHpHd7rpa42i9grFk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"Retime load/store lane metadata|load/store lane metadata|mem_misalign|byte_mask|aligned_addr","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 1 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 11: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Retime load/store lane metadata\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\\nextraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\\nloads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\\nraise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\\nextraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\\nloads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\\nraise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute and carry the load/store lane metadata out of EX: word-aligned\\naddress, byte mask, and byte-lane shift/selection can be latched with the\\nEX/MEM payload so MEM only has to perform the actual memory access and a\\nmuch smaller extract/extend step. This should reduce the hot memory-path\\nlogic seen by synthesis while preserving retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the lane metadata once the ALU result is known so the memory stage no longer needs to decode width/address details.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried metadata to simplify byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic on the MEM critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the lane metadata once the ALU result is known so the memory stage no longer needs ...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"Retime load/store lane metadata|load/store lane metadata|mem_misalign|byte_mask|aligned_addr","time":{"start":1778871568773,"end":1778871568779}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0d45fb20454bf973016a076d109c44819b854d9e7c09e43ec3"}},"id":"prt_e2d02096f001rGNSPd7CIEezhm","sessionID":"ses_1d2fe3047ffeNwTumIICkSX4cE","messageID":"msg_e2d01e88e001xNaPioYt7xf0Bq"}}
