sis\": \"Keep the one-cycle ALU for ADD/SUB/logic/shifts and the multiply ops, but\\nmove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a small iterative side unit that only stalls the\\npipe when a divide is actually executing. Expose the divide result back\\nthrough the existing EX/WB retirement path and preserve the RV32M corner\\ncases exactly. This is a pure structural split that should shrink the common\\ncritical path while leaving non-divide CoreMark code on the fast path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the divider/remainder combinational cone from the common ALU path and keep the fast integer/multiply ops single-cycle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small iterative divider/remainder engine that returns RV32M-correct results and handles divide-by-zero and overflow cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route DIV/REM instructions into the divider unit and hold the EX/MEM state until the result is ready.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an active divide as a pipeline stall source so younger instructions do not advance while the divider r... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry hot-branch predictor in IF that stores one recently\\nresolved taken B-type/JAL PC, its target, and a valid bit. On a PC match,\\nfetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through and let the\\nexisting EX redirect train the entry from the resolved path. Keep JALR and\\nlegality checks off the predictor fast path so the hardware stays small\\nenough for Tang Nano 20K and the formal state stays bounded.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 335.7, \"delta_pct... (line truncated to 2000 chars)","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","time":{"start":1778871575110,"end":1778871575116}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_00e5be853154e896016a076d1701e0819baa7b34d02f52920e"}},"id":"prt_e2d022243001HWRKMwrXFduafu","sessionID":"ses_1d2fe3047ffeNwTumIICkSX4cE","messageID":"msg_e2d020a27001cTX2kS7ZKUIyqB"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778871575136,"sessionID":"ses_1d2fe3047ffeNwTumIICkSX4cE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_A70SwTd22zjtxt35tKQ2NFQX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","offset":13,"limit":5},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n13: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry hot-branch predictor in IF that stores one recently\\nresolved taken B-type/JAL PC, its target, and a valid bit. On a PC match,\\nfetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through and let the\\nexisting EX redirect train the entry from the resolved path. Keep JALR and\\nlegality checks off the predictor fast path so the hardware stays small\\nenough for Tang Nano 20K and the formal state stays bounded.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 335.7, \"delta_pct... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n14: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Predecode hot instruction fields\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current decode path fans the full 32-bit instruction into legality,\\nregister address extraction, and hazard checks. On a small FPGA, that\\nrepeated slicing and nested opcode logic is a plausible Fmax limiter once\\nthe branch-target cone has already been trimmed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current decode path fans the full 32-bit instruction into legality,\\nregister address extraction, and hazard checks. On a small FPGA, that\\nrepeated slicing and nested opcode logic is a plausible Fmax limiter once\\nthe branch-target cone has already been trimmed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move instruction-field extraction to the IF/ID boundary: latch opcode,\\nfunct3, funct7, rd, rs1, rs2, and EBREAK qualification in the pipeline\\nbundle, then have `decoder` and `hazard_unit` consume those predecoded\\nfields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction word. This should cut\\ndecode fanout and simplify the common ID critical path without changing\\nISA-visible behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predecoded IF/ID sideband fields for opcode/funct/register-address metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Extract and latch the instruction metadata once when fetching, including EBREAK qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrower predecoded fields instead of repeatedly slicing the raw instruction bus.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the latched source register addresses from IF/ID so load-use checks stop fanning out the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the new predecoded bundle through decode and keep the ID/EX register semantics unchanged.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n15: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Early branch resolution\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage still carries branch compare, redirect selection, and the\\nforwarding muxes on the same path. CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight\\nloops, so taking conditional branches off that cone should help both Fmax\\nand the loop-throughput side of the fitness score.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage still carries branch compare, redirect selection, and the\\nforwarding muxes on the same path. CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight\\nloops, so taking conditional branches off that cone should help both Fmax\\nand the loop-throughput side of the fitness score.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move B-type branch resolution into ID so BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU can\\nredirect one stage earlier, while leaving JALR in EX to preserve the\\nfreshness guarantees on rs1. The common case then stops paying branch\\ncompare cost in EX, and the hot redirect path becomes shorter without\\nchanging architectural results.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retarget operand selection so ID can see fresher rs1/rs2 values for conditional branch compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve conditional branch compare and misalignment checks in decode, then emit the early redirect information.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove branch compare work from the hot EX cone and keep JALR plus non-branch ALU work on the live execute path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect control so the ID-stage branch resolver can drive fetch without waiting for EX on B-type branches.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retarget operand selection so ID can see fresher rs1/rs2 values for conditional branch compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"descri... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n16: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny return-address stack\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark and its library calls spend meaningful time in call/return\\ntraffic, and this core still resolves every JALR return after fetch.\\nA bounded return predictor can cut those recurring wrong-path flushes\\nwithout dragging a general BTB or branch-immediate decode into IF.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark and its library calls spend meaningful time in call/return\\ntraffic, and this core still resolves every JALR return after fetch.\\nA bounded return predictor can cut those recurring wrong-path flushes\\nwithout dragging a general BTB or branch-immediate decode into IF.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small return-address stack that predicts JALR returns from\\nthe common link-register pattern and trains only on resolved JAL/JALR\\ncontrol flow. Keep the predictor state bounded and the fetch-side check\\nsimple, so IF uses only opcode/rd/rs1 bits already present in the fetched\\ninstruction while EX remains the source of truth for updates and\\nmispredict recovery.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack and use it to choose the predicted next PC for return-like JALR fetches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate predictor update metadata from resolved JAL/JALR control flow and redirect on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the predictor update signals between EX and IF without changing the RVFI or memory IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack and use it to choose the predicted next PC for return-like JALR fetches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate predictor update metadata from resolved JAL/JALR control flow and redirect on mispredict... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 16 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \