{"type":"text","timestamp":1778875344901,"sessionID":"ses_1d2c52abcffekpDYdu688CjsZH","part":{"id":"prt_e2d3ba7bf001WaPYS4CVRHDNht","messageID":"msg_e2d3b85d9002oKLKRFj5QX6VzZ","sessionID":"ses_1d2c52abcffekpDYdu688CjsZH","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis now. It stays within the existing pipeline contract and only narrows compare work on dead source operands.","time":{"start":1778875344831,"end":1778875344899},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0fdd6c6bb367b526016a077bd0b98c819bbac6e6873b220038","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778875348663,"sessionID":"ses_1d2c52abcffekpDYdu688CjsZH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_1WlrlsqtUolrHSkRMwrSDBQW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r9s0\n+title: \"Source-use mask\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends much of its time on op-imm, loads, and simple control\n+  flow, yet the core still evaluates both forwarding compare trees and the\n+  load-use hazard compare on every cycle. On a small FPGA, those dead\n+  equality chains and their fanout are a plausible Fmax limiter even when\n+  the ISA behavior is already correct.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add compact source-operand-use flags to the decoded control bundle and use\n+  them to gate only the compare trees for operands the current instruction\n+  cannot read. That lets forwarding and load-use detection skip the rs2 path\n+  for immediate-style and other single-source instructions while preserving\n+  the existing retirement semantics, forwarding priority, and stall rules.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact source-use flags to the decoded control bundle so later stages can tell whether rs1 and rs2 are live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the source-use flags for each opcode class while keeping the existing legality and control decode unchanged.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the new source-use flags into the ID/EX register alongside the existing decoded control bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Gate the rs1/rs2 equality trees with the live-source flags so dead operands do not pay for compare work.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Use the same live-source flags to skip unnecessary load-use comparisons on instructions that cannot consume a given source register.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r9s0.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-001-r9s0\n+title: \"Source-use mask\"\n+category: micro_opt\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends much of its time on op-imm, loads, and simple control\n+  flow, yet the core still evaluates both forwarding compare trees and the\n+  load-use hazard compare on every cycle. On a small FPGA, those dead\n+  equality chains and their fanout are a plausible Fmax limiter even when\n+  the ISA behavior is already correct.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add compact source-operand-use flags to the decoded control bundle and use\n+  them to gate only the compare trees for operands the current instruction\n+  cannot read. That lets forwarding and load-use detection skip the rs2 path\n+  for immediate-style and other single-source instructions while preserving\n+  the existing retirement semantics, forwarding priority, and stall rules.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact source-use flags to the decoded control bundle so later stages can tell whether rs1 and rs2 are live.\"\n+  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the source-use flags f