ting legality and control decode unchanged.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the new source-use flags into the ID/EX register alongside the existing decoded control bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Gate the rs1/rs2 equality trees with the live-source flags so dead operands do not pay for compare work.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the same live-source flags to skip unnecessary load-use co...\n  Line 27: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r9s1\", \"title\": \"Split RV32M from ALU\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU computes RV32M products and quotients inside the same\\ncombinational block as ADD/SUB/logic/shift work. That makes the execute\\npath wider than it needs to be, even on instructions that never use the\\nM-extension.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU computes RV32M products and quotients inside the same\\ncombinational block as ADD/SUB/logic/shift work. That makes the execute\\npath wider than it needs to be, even on instructions that never use the\\nM-extension.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a dedicated RV32M side\\nunit so the common integer ALU only carries RV32I operations. Keep the\\nmultiply path single-cycle if the FPGA maps it well, and let DIV/REM use a\\nsmall stalled engine; this should shrink the hot EX cone without changing\\narchitectural results.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove RV32M execution from the common ALU datapath and keep the module focused on RV32I arithmetic and logic.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route M-extension ops into the dedicated side unit and preserve the existing retirement/writeback behavior.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat a busy divide path as a stall source so t