{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778877991077,"sessionID":"ses_1d29c3be4ffea5larosxWK1oND","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_DMeA2GT6J59ASbEcNzJuTh27","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\"","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments","include":"log.jsonl"},"output":"Found 1 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 12: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split divide from ALU\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps the full RV32M divide/remainder logic in the common\\ncombinational datapath. That is expensive logic on a small FPGA, even though\\nCoreMark is much more branch- and multiply-heavy than divide-heavy. Removing\\nDIV/REM from the hot ALU cone should raise Fmax without changing the ISA-\\nvisible result stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps the full RV32M divide/remainder logic in the common\\ncombinational datapath. That is expensive logic on a small FPGA, even though\\nCoreMark is much more branch- and multiply-heavy than divide-heavy. Removing\\nDIV/REM from the hot ALU cone should raise Fmax without changing the ISA-\\nvisible result stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the one-cycle ALU for ADD/SUB/logic/shifts and the multiply ops, but\\nmove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a small iterative side unit that only stalls the\\npipe when a divide is actually executing. Expose the divide result back\\nthrough the existing EX/WB retirement path and preserve the RV32M corner\\ncases exactly. This is a pure structural split that should shrink the common\\ncritical path while leaving non-divide CoreMark code on the fast path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the divider/remainder combinational cone from the common ALU path and keep the fast integer/multiply ops single-cycle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small iterative divider/remainder engine that returns RV32M-correct results and handles divide-by-zero and overflow cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route DIV/REM instructions into the divider unit and hold the EX/MEM state until the result is ready.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an active divide as a pipeline stall source so younger instructions do not advance while the divider r...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\"","time":{"start":1778877991058,"end":1778877991076}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07bc690f1a22a33a016a078626ec94819a8fd32e51fb126a17"}},"id":"prt_e2d64087f001H3DOLRsZrBnviU","sessionID":"ses_1d29c3be4ffea5larosxWK1oND","messageID":"msg_e2d63d9aa001PGzv6UKloWrFKJ"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778877991078,"sessionID":"ses_1d29c3be4ffea5larosxWK1oND","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_0I1x7tsQ0nEstQvYLne3waoT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r10s1\"","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments","include":"log.jsonl"},"output":"Found 1 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 30: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed fetch boundary\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The remaining hot path is likely the combinational fetch-to-decode loop,\\nwhere `imem_data` still fans into decode, hazard checks, and PC control in\\nthe same cycle. Breaking that boundary should give synthesis a cleaner\\nstage cut than another fetch-side predictor, especially after the branch\\ntarget work already moved earlier.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The remaining hot path is likely the combinational fetch-to-decode loop,\\nwhere `imem_data` still fans into decode, hazard checks, and PC control in\\nthe same cycle. Breaking that boundary should give synthesis a cleaner\\nstage cut than another fetch-side predictor, especially after the branch\\ntarget work already moved earlier.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Insert a real IF/ID register so fetched instructions are latched once\\nbefore decode and hazard logic see them. That should shorten the\\nimem-to-decode-to-flush feedback cone and reduce the amount of logic that\\nsits on the fetch critical path, while preserving the architectural\\nretirement stream and existing stall/redirect rules.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Retimes fetch through a registered IF/ID boundary so the PC update path no longer feeds decode combinationally in the same cycle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched fetch bundle as the decode input and keep the existing decode, operand read, and ID/EX semantics aligned to the new boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the registered IF/ID view for load-use checks so stall generation no longer sits on the same combinational fetch path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire the top-level stage boundary for the new fetch register while preserving the RVFI and memory I/O contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r10s1\"","time":{"start":1778877991061,"end":1778877991078}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07bc690f1a22a33a016a078626eca8819a8532bf345bcd3342"}},"id":"prt_e2d640894001T53QrEQMmJGZAU","sessionID":"ses_1d29c3be4ffea5larosxWK1oND","messageID":"msg_e2d63d9aa001PGzv6UKloWrFKJ"}}
