{"type":"text","timestamp":1778884198804,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","part":{"id":"prt_e2dc2beac001zyAtmx3heCUvqT","messageID":"msg_e2dc286e2001Ou0gYApeoM454Z","sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","type":"text","text":"I checked the experiment directory. There’s already a sibling slot for this round, so I’m reading that briefly to avoid duplicating the same idea.","time":{"start":1778884198060,"end":1778884198803},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0b9089d2859a45f6016a079e65de708199bb0eed6196a87f19","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778884198850,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_OcbPX6ZLWC9ifmHI1tEO7dN1","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\n2: title: \"Gate always-on multiplier work\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark spends most cycles on non-M instructions, but the current ALU still\n6:   computes three 64-bit products on every cycle before the opcode case selects\n7:   a result. That keeps multiplier fanout in the common execute cone even when\n8:   the instruction is just ADD, LOAD, BRANCH, or a shift.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Move the 64-bit product generation behind the M-extension arm so the common\n11:   non-M path does not pay for always-on multiply logic. Keep the ALTOPS branch\n12:   and the real RV32M branch behaviorally identical, but let synthesis see a\n13:   smaller fast path for the instructions CoreMark executes most often.\n14: expected_impact:\n15:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\n16:   confidence: medium\n17: changes:\n18:   - file: rtl/alu.sv\n19:     description: \"Compute the signed and unsigned 64-bit products only when an M-extension opcode is selected, while preserving the existing ALTOPS and real-arithmetic results.\"\n\n(End of file - total 19 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\ntitle: \"Gate always-on multiplier work\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark spends most cycles on non-M instructions, but the current ALU still\n  computes three 64-bit products on every cycle before the opcode case selects\n  a result. That keeps multiplier fanout in the common execute cone even when\n  the instruction is just ADD, LOAD, BRANCH, or a shift.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move the 64-bit product generation behind the M-extension arm so the common\n  non-M path does not pay for always-on multiply logic. Keep the ALTOPS branch\n  and the real RV32M branch behaviorally identical, but let synthesis see a\n  smaller fast path for the instructions CoreMark executes most often.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Compute the signed and unsigned 64-bit products only when an M-extension opcode is selected, while preserving the existing ALTOPS and real-arithmetic results.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r13s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778884198820,"end":1778884198849}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b9089d2859a45f6016a079e66b55c8199a8e46019f15e53e7"}},"id":"prt_e2dc2c194001uh6GvdinW3YmG4","sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","messageID":"msg_e2dc286e2001Ou0gYApeoM454Z"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778884198866,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_lZg0imAm8EnEfLX9WIr5tvv3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-002-r13s1.log","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20260515-002-r13s1.log</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778884113809,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2dc1758f0010m505VBU9yO1xx\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2dc170b0001z8ZqIbMyEXlXuf\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"snapshot\":\"2e7a3e6d778f0e1294d2420335e430bb2b430600\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n2: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778884116996,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2dc17e8f001WNHIfVWQ2CMsR8\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2dc170b0001z8ZqIbMyEXlXuf\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I’m checking the prior attempts and lessons first so the hypothesis targets a gap instead of rehashing a known regression.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778884116111,\"end\":1778884116994},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0d1426027bcbc10f016a079e13f64c819a86b851ac49ce6243\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n3: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778884117109,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_B0LR7A9LQZsnUnNJVd378VG1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":400},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (broken, n/a): Moving control-flow target math earlier only works if JALR still sees the freshest rs1 value; precomputing jump targets without airtight forwarding/stalling breaks formal on taken-jump semantics.\\n2:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r1s1 (improvement, +18.70%): Precomputing BRANCH/JAL targets in ID can materially improve Fmax by cutting the EX-to-IF redirect cone, but the live JALR path still has to stay in EX because it depends on forwarded rs1 data.\\n3:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.50%): A tiny static backward-branch predictor can still lose on a loop-heavy benchmark if the branch-immediate decode and legality checks extend the IF critical path more than the saved EX redirect flushes.\\n4:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r3s2 (broken, n/a): Even a tiny direct-mapped BTB can make formal blow past wall-clock limits, so fetch-side predictor state needs proof-time budgeting as well as performance tuning.\\n5:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r5s0 (regression, -13.60%): Predecoding opcode/funct/register fields into the IF/ID bundle only helps if decode slicing was the dominant cost; on a small FPGA, widening the fetch-side combinational payload can cost more Fmax than the ID fanout it removes.\\n6:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r6s0 (improvement, +1.16%): Carrying predecoded load/store lane metadata (aligned address, byte mask, shift, and misalign flag) from EX into MEM trims the memory-side combina... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778884117128,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_Kl2x4teFsVZPKshz2Cgc3Kx5\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"structural|fetch buffer|retire snapshot|RAS|predictor|pipeline|fanout\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\",\"include\":\"*.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 33 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Retime control-flow arithmetic\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \\\"Move common control-flow arithmetic earlier in the pipe: carry a precomputed PC+4 value forward from fetch, precompute branch and JALR targets in decode, and let EX only perform the branch compare plus a small target select. This should shorten the EX critical path and raise clock speed without changing retirement semantics.\\\\n\\\", \\\"expected_impact\\\": {\\\"fitness_delta_pct\\\": 5, \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\"}, \\\"changes\\\": [{\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/core_pkg.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rtl/if_stage.sv\\\", \\\"description\\\": \\\"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\\\"}, {\\\"file\\\": \\\"rt... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n5: {\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1778884117251,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2dc182ff001inEuJ7MT5kyKcQ\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"2e7a3e6d778f0e1294d2420335e430bb2b430600\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2dc170b0001z8ZqIbMyEXlXuf\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":39614,\"input\":39134,\"output\":195,\"reasoning\":285,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":0}},\"cost\":0}}\n6: {\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778884118505,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2dc187e5001TSBkQ3fCjetkmP\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2dc18371001XusXPrD6660BEo\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"snapshot\":\"2e7a3e6d778f0e1294d2420335e430bb2b430600\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n7: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778884180787,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2dc27a620013aRnVGv6cwDc2C\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2dc18371001XusXPrD6660BEo\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I’ve got the likely direction: a corrected atomic fetch-latch retime, because the current front-end still looks like the best remaining structural bottleneck and the prior failure was from bundle semantics, not the idea itself.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778884180578,\"end\":1778884180786},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_03435d16f7c15a5b016a079e546a00819aa894c71e344427da\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n8: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778884180837,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"glob\",\"callID\":\"call_lSecl67WpDKvhcV1FCVz2ULM\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1\"},\"output\":\"No files found\",\"metadata\":{\"count\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778884180810,\"end\":1778884180836}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_03435d16f7c15a5b016a079e54a758819a8e63ace56bce074f\"}},\"id\":\"prt_e2dc27b340010