content>\\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\\n2: title: \\\"Gate always-on multiplier work\\\"\\n3: category: micro_opt\\n4: motivation: |\\n5:   CoreMark spends most cycles on non-M instructions, but the current ALU still\\n6:   computes three 64-bit products on every cycle before the opcode case selects\\n7:   a result. That keeps multiplier fanout in the common execute cone even when\\n8:   the instruction is just ADD, LOAD, BRANCH, or a shift.\\n9: hypothesis: |\\n10:   Move the 64-bit product generation behind the M-extension arm so the common\\n11:   non-M path does not pay for always-on multiply logic. Keep the ALTOPS branch\\n12:   and the real RV32M branch behaviorally identical, but let synthesis see a\\n13:   smaller fast path for the instructions CoreMark executes most often.\\n14: expected_impact:\\n15:   fitness_delta_pct: 4\\n16:   confidence: medium\\n17: changes:\\n18:   - file: rtl/alu.sv\\n19:     description: \\\"Compute the signed and unsigned 64-bit products only when an M-extension opcode is selected, while preserving the existing ALTOPS and real-arithmetic results.\\\"\\n\\n(End of file - total 19 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"id: hyp-20260515-001-r13s0\\ntitle: \\\"Gate always-on multiplier work\\\"\\ncategory: micro_opt\\nmotivation: |\\n  CoreMark spends most cycles on non-M instructions, but the current ALU still\\n  computes three 64-bit products on every cycle before the opcode case selects\\n  a resu... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 17 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1778884113809,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2dc1758f0010m505VBU9yO1xx\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2dc170b0001z8ZqIbMyEXlXuf\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"snapshot\":\"2e7a3e6d778f0e1294d2420335e430bb2b430600\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1778884116996,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e2dc17e8f001WNHIfVWQ2CMsR8\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e2dc170b0001z8ZqIbMyEXlXuf\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I’m checking the prior attempts and lessons first so the hypothesis targets a gap instead of rehashing a known regression.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1778884116111,\"end\":1778884116994},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0d1426027bcbc10f016a079e13f64c819a86b851ac49ce6243\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778884117109,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_B0LR7A9LQZsnUnNJVd378VG1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":400},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/LESSONS.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r1s0 (broken, n/a): Moving control-flow target math earlier only works if JALR still sees the freshest rs1 value; precomputing jump targets without airtight forwarding/stalling breaks formal on taken-jump semantics.\\n2:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-002-r1s1 (improvement, +18.70%): Precomputing BRANCH/JAL targets in ID can materially improve Fmax by cutting the EX-to-IF redirect cone, but the live JALR path still has to stay in EX because it depends on forwarded rs1 data.\\n3:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.50%): A tiny static backward-branch predictor can still lose on a loop-heavy benchmark if the branch-immediate decode and legality checks extend the IF critical path more than the saved EX redirect flushes.\\n4:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-003-r3s2 (broken, n/a): Even a tiny direct-mapped BTB can make formal blow past wall-clock limits, so fetch-side predictor state needs proof-time budgeting as well as performance tuning.\\n5:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r5s0 (regression, -13.60%): Predecoding opcode/funct/register fields into the IF/ID bundle only helps if decode slicing was the dominant cost; on a small FPGA, widening the fetch-side combinational payload can cost more Fmax than the ID fanout it removes.\\n6:   - 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r6s0 (improvement, +1.16%): Carrying predecoded load/store lane metadata (aligned address, byte mask, shift, and misalign flag) from EX into MEM trims the memory-side combina... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1778884117128,\"sessionID\":\"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_Kl2x4teFsVZPKshz2Cgc3Kx5\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"structural|fetch buffer|retire snapshot|RAS|predictor|pipeline|fanout\",\"path\":\"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\",\"include\":\"*.jsonl\"},\"output\":\"Found 33 matches\\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\\n  Line 2: {\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Retime control-flow arithmetic\\\", \\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\", \\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": \