{"type":"text","timestamp":1778884212132,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","part":{"id":"prt_e2dc2f4f90011lh649tH0az0He","messageID":"msg_e2dc2c2d9001XdwsKCnHT3j6iy","sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis file now. I’m keeping it narrow: one structural retime of the front end, with the atomic-bundle detail called out so it doesn’t repeat the prior broken fetch-buffer shape.","time":{"start":1778884211961,"end":1778884212131},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0a3ba689b64a2a21016a079e73d2e88199a27ef8460690add9","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778884213550,"sessionID":"ses_1d23e8ff8ffe2Ku6HH4E3kmiaj","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_PVJJRDx477qqpps5QuXRa72i","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r13s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r13s1\n+title: \"Atomic fetch latch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The front end still exposes a wide combinational `pc`/`instr`/`valid`\n+  bundle to decode and hazard logic in the same cycle that fetch updates\n+  the PC. On this small FPGA, that fetch-to-decode feedback cone is one of\n+  the few remaining structural paths left to retime after the control-flow\n+  predictor work.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Replace the purely combinational fetch-facing bundle with a real atomic\n+  IF/ID latch that updates `pc`, `instr`, `valid`, and the prediction sideband\n+  together on stall, flush, and redirect. Keep decode and hazard checks\n+  consuming only the latched bundle so no stage still depends on raw\n+  `imem_data` in the same cycle. This should shorten the front-end critical\n+  path without changing the architectural retirement stream.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Turn fetch into the sole owner of an atomic IF/ID latch so `pc`, `instr`, `valid`, and prediction sideband fields update together on stall/flush/redirect.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the registered fetch bundle unchanged and avoid any new dependence on raw `imem_data` in decode.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Keep load-use detection and stall generation on the latched instruction bundle rather than the live fetch cone.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r13s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r13s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r13s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r13s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r13s1\n+title: \"Atomic fetch latch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The front end still exposes a wide combinational `pc`/`instr`/`valid`\n+  bundle to decode and hazard logic in the same cycle that fetch updates\n+  the PC. On this small FPGA, that fetch-to-decode feedback cone is one of\n+  the few remaining structural paths left to retime after the control-flow\n+  predictor work.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Replace the purely combinational fetch-facing bundle with a real atomic\n+  IF/ID latch that updates `pc`, `instr`, `valid`, and the prediction sideband\n+  together on stall, flush, and redirect. Keep decode and hazard checks\n+  consuming only the latched bundle so no stage still depends on raw\n+  `imem_data` in the same cycle. This should shorten the front-end critical\n+  path without changing the architectural retirement stream.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Turn fetch into the sole owner of an atomic IF/ID latch so `pc`, `instr`, `valid`, and prediction sideband fields update together on stall/flush/redirect.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the registered fetch bundle unchanged and avoid any new dependence on raw `imem_data` in decode.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Keep load-use detection and stall generation on the latched instruction bundle rather than the live fetch cone.\"\n\n","files":[{"