{"type":"text","timestamp":1778886232450,"sessionID":"ses_1d21e7c28ffee2JvzTj4W7Ptvw","part":{"id":"prt_e2de1c5d40018OhYXxuWvd7WgM","messageID":"msg_e2de1b376001LryChQg290OlbH","sessionID":"ses_1d21e7c28ffee2JvzTj4W7Ptvw","type":"text","text":"I’ve got the prior attempt history; now I’m checking whether the operand-bypass retiming path actually failed or just wasn’t curated into the lessons, since that’s the cleanest remaining structural lever.","time":{"start":1778886231508,"end":1778886232449},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0b4519bf9262d337016a07a657696c819885ae4f38c7f8e504","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778886232463,"sessionID":"ses_1d21e7c28ffee2JvzTj4W7Ptvw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_PmIaFPLLDtfjXiG4vD1oEB0e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"hyp-20260515-003-r3s1|retimed operand bypass|operand bypass","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 1 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass selection into ID, latch already-forwarded\\nrs1/rs2 values in the ID/EX register, and let EX consume stable operands\\ndirectly. Keep the existing load-use stall rule and x0 filtering intact so\\ncorrectness stays the same while the EX combinational cone gets shorter.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwarding before the ID/EX flop and latch the selected operands into the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume pre-forwarded operands directly and drop the operand-select muxes from the EX critical path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retime or simplify bypass selection so it serves the ID-side operand latch instead of EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwardin...","metadata":{"matches":1,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260515-003-r3s1|retimed operand bypass|operand bypass","time":{"start":1778886232452,"end":1778886232462}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b4519bf9262d337016a07a658595c8198abe8cf6e1d3fca5e"}},"id":"prt_e2de1c983001eoImQTeEqfsw9u","sessionID":"ses_1d21e7c28ffee2JvzTj4W7Ptvw","messageID":"msg_e2de1b376001LryChQg290OlbH"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778886232495,"sessionID":"ses_1d21e7c28ffee2JvzTj4W7Ptvw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_oq3idiqGZ3nB7oaddaf3Sf7o","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"hyp-20260515-002-r13s1|atomic fetch latch|fetch buffer|IF/ID latch","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 2 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 36: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r12s1\", \"title\": \"Add a fetch buffer\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The front end still lets `imem_data` fan into PC selection, decode, and\\nhazard checks in one cycle. That creates a wide fetch-to-decode cone on a\\nsmall FPGA, even after the earlier branch-target and predictor experiments.\\nA tiny registered fetch buffer should cut that cone without changing the\\narchitectural retirement stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The front end still lets `imem_data` fan into PC selection, decode, and\\nhazard checks in one cycle. That creates a wide fetch-to-decode cone on a\\nsmall FPGA, even after the earlier branch-target and predictor experiments.\\nA tiny registered fetch buffer should cut that cone without changing the\\narchitectural retirement stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a one-entry fetch buffer that latches the fetched `pc`, `instr`, and\\nvalid bit before decode consumes them, while keeping the PC engine and\\nredirect logic on a narrower path. This should decouple the fetch timing\\nfrom the decode/hazard fanout, reduce the hot combinational span through the\\nfront end, and preserve the existing stall, flush, and RVFI behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry fetch buffer and separate the PC update path from the decode-facing output bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the buffered fetch bundle unchanged so decode and immediate generation stay aligned to the new boundary.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire the top-level front end around the buffered fetch stage without changing the external I/O or RVFI contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry fetch buffer and separate the PC update path from the decode-facing output bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", ...\n  Line 39: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r13s1\", \"title\": \"Atomic fetch latch\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The front end still exposes a wide combinational `pc`/`instr`/`valid`\\nbundle to decode and hazard logic in the same cycle that fetch updates\\nthe PC. On this small FPGA, that fetch-to-decode feedback cone is one of\\nthe few remaining structural paths left to retime after the control-flow\\npredictor work.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The front end still exposes a wide combinational `pc`/`instr`/`valid`\\nbundle to decode and hazard logic in the same cycle that fetch updates\\nthe PC. On this small FPGA, that fetch-to-decode feedback cone is one of\\nthe few remaining structural paths left to retime after the control-flow\\npredictor work.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the purely combinational fetch-facing bundle with a real atomic\\nIF/ID latch that updates `pc`, `instr`, `valid`, and the prediction sideband\\ntogether on stall, flush, and redirect. Keep decode and hazard checks\\nconsuming only the latched bundle so no stage still depends on raw\\n`imem_data` in the same cycle. This should shorten the front-end critical\\npath without changing the architectural retirement stream.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn fetch into the sole owner of an atomic IF/ID latch so `pc`, `instr`, `valid`, and prediction sideband fields update together on stall/flush/redirect.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the registered fetch bundle unchanged and avoid any new dependence on raw `imem_data` in decode.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep load-use detection and stall generation on the latched instruction bundle rather than the live fetch cone.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Turn fetch into the sole owner of an atomic IF/ID latch so `pc`, `instr`, `v...","metadata":{"matches":2,"truncated":false},"title":"hyp-20260515-002-r13s1|atomic fetch latch|fetch buffer|IF/ID latch","time":{"start":1778886232476,"end":1778886232493}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0b4519bf9262d337016a07a658596c819883e18f78aa5589ae"}},"id":"prt_e2de1c99a001O6mEwiVO6Uzj7K","sessionID":"ses_1d21e7c28ffee2JvzTj4W7Ptvw","messageID":"msg_e2de1b376001LryChQg290OlbH"}}
