{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778886302392,"sessionID":"ses_1d21e7c28ffee2JvzTj4W7Ptvw","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_4MouEKEcNwNwvkBHKj1YYa99","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r14s1\n+title: \"ID-side bypass latch\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  EX still pays for bypass selection on every instruction, even when the\n+  operation is a simple ALU op or a branch compare. Retiming that mux work\n+  into ID should shrink the common execute cone while leaving the ISA-visible\n+  retirement stream unchanged.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Resolve EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding in ID, latch the selected rs1/rs2\n+  values into the ID/EX register, and let EX consume stable operands directly.\n+  Keep x0 filtering and the existing load-use stall rule intact so freshness\n+  stays correct while the hot EX bypass muxes disappear.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Thread forwarding selects into ID and remove the EX-stage bypass wiring from the top-level path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a forwarding-aware operand latch so ID captures already-selected rs1/rs2 values before the ID/EX flop.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Keep the compare logic but retarget the bypass outputs to feed ID-side operand selection.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the stable operands directly and drop the hot bypass muxes from the EX combinational cone.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r14s1.yaml\n========================