02-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Dedicated effective-address fast path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Loads, stores, and JALR all currently route base-plus-offset address formation through the same EX datapath that also serves arithmetic and branch work. On a small FPGA, that shared cone is a natural Fmax limiter, especially in a CoreMark mix with frequent memory traffic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Loads, stores, and JALR all currently route base-plus-offset address formation through the same EX datapath that also serves arithmetic and branch work. On a small FPGA, that shared cone is a natural Fmax limiter, especially in a CoreMark mix with frequent memory traffic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a dedicated effective-address adder in EX for LOAD, STORE, and JALR, and carry its result as a separate EX/MEM sideband so the main ALU only handles true arithmetic and logic ops. MEM then consumes the sideband directly for address, alignment, and RVFI memory fields. This should shorten the hot execute path without changing architectural retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an EX/MEM sideband field for the dedicated effective-address result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute LOAD/STORE/JALR addresses with a separate adder instead of routing them through the main ALU cone.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried effective-address sideband for memory access and RVFI memory reporting.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an EX/MEM sideband field for the dedicated effective-address result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute LOAD/STORE/JALR addresses with a separate adder instead of routing them through the main ALU con