{"type":"text","timestamp":1778889296294,"sessionID":"ses_1d1f07a54ffeDPpM1OmIIRz022","part":{"id":"prt_e2e108925001pC9tvF3ow46Ubj","messageID":"msg_e2e1065500013YM59CLulmc7P6","sessionID":"ses_1d1f07a54ffeDPpM1OmIIRz022","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis file now. I’m keeping it narrow: a two-entry atomic fetch skid buffer to retime the front end without changing the retirement contract.","time":{"start":1778889296165,"end":1778889296293},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0a449bc9c33438fe016a07b25003dc819a802d7152d97f2fde","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778889298276,"sessionID":"ses_1d1f07a54ffeDPpM1OmIIRz022","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_soffDSJdiw3o5zY6iXpqwdmJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r15s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r15s1\n+title: \"Two-entry fetch skid buffer\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The remaining hot path is still the fetch-to-decode feedback cone, where\n+  `imem_data` fans into control flow, decode, and hazard logic in the same\n+  cycle. A tiny registered skid buffer should give synthesis a cleaner stage\n+  cut on this small FPGA without changing the ISA-visible retirement stream.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a two-entry atomic fetch skid buffer that holds `pc`, `instr`, `valid`,\n+  and prediction sideband state together before decode consumes them. Let IF\n+  own the queue and PC update path, and let ID/hazard logic see only the\n+  buffered head entry. This should shorten the front-end critical path more\n+  safely than a pure combinational fetch bundle or a one-entry latch.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add the two-entry atomic fetch skid buffer and keep the PC/redirect path separate from the decode-facing head entry.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume the buffered fetch head unchanged so decode and immediate generation stay aligned to the new boundary.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Rewire the top-level front end around the buffered fetch stage without changing the external I/O or RVFI contract.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r15s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-0