{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778854720822,"sessionID":"ses_1d4015a39ffeCeg59I07ZGndUV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_2OZ0UCxg2zWYFgI4HIGs2Wgj","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\n+title: \"Retimed operand bypass\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\n+  instruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\n+  compare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\n+  shrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass selection into ID, latch already-forwarded\n+  rs1/rs2 values in the ID/EX register, and let EX consume stable operands\n+  directly. Keep the existing load-use stall rule and x0 filtering intact so\n+  correctness stays the same while the EX combinational cone gets shorter.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwarding before the ID/EX flop and latch the selected operands into the pipeline register.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume pre-forwarded operands directly and drop the operand-select muxes from the EX critical path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Retime or simplify bypass selection so it serves the ID-side operand latch instead of EX.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r3s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypothe