edium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 335.7, \"delta_pct... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 13 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split divide from ALU\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps the full RV32M divide/remainder logic in the common\\ncombinational datapath. That is expensive logic on a small FPGA, even though\\nCoreMark is much more branch- and multiply-heavy than divide-heavy. Removing\\nDIV/REM from the hot ALU cone should raise Fmax without changing the ISA-\\nvisible result stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps the full RV32M divide/remainder logic in the common\\ncombinational datapath. That is expensive logic on a small FPGA, even though\\nCoreMark is much more branch- and multiply-heavy than divide-heavy. Removing\\nDIV/REM from the hot ALU cone should raise Fmax without changing the ISA-\\nvisible result stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the one-cycle ALU for ADD/SUB/logic/shifts and the multiply ops, but\\nmove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a small iterative side unit that only stalls the\\npipe when a divide is actually executing. Expose the divide result back\\nthrough the existing EX/WB retirement path and preserve the