{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778869766909,"sessionID":"ses_1d31b648effeA8mDo9o8jtu6V6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_dIIk708j6x93xVC0iPqR42jU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r5s1\n+title: \"Early branch resolution\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The EX stage still carries branch compare, redirect selection, and the\n+  forwarding muxes on the same path. CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight\n+  loops, so taking conditional branches off that cone should help both Fmax\n+  and the loop-throughput side of the fitness score.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move B-type branch resolution into ID so BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU can\n+  redirect one stage earlier, while leaving JALR in EX to preserve the\n+  freshness guarantees on rs1. The common case then stops paying branch\n+  compare cost in EX, and the hot redirect path becomes shorter without\n+  changing architectural results.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add any branch-resolution sideband fields needed to carry an early compare result cleanly through the pipeline.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Resolve conditional branch compare and misalignment checks in decode, then emit the early redirect information.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Remove branch compare work from the hot EX cone and keep JALR plus non-branch ALU work on the live execute path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Rewire redirect control so the ID-stage branch resolver can drive fetch without waiting for EX on B-type branches.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r5s1.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r5s1\n+title: \"Early branch resolution\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The EX stage still carries branch compare, redirect selection, and the\n+  forwarding muxes on the same path. CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight\n+  loops, so taking conditional branches off that cone should help both Fmax\n+  and the loop-throughput side of the fitness score.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move B-type branch resolution into ID so BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU can\n+  redirect one stage earlier, while leaving JALR in EX to preserve the\n+  freshness guarantees on rs1. The common case then stops paying branch\n+  compare cost in EX, and the hot redirect path becomes shorter without\n+  changing architectural results.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add any branch-resolution sideband fields needed to carry an early compare result cleanly through the pipeline.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Resolve conditional branch compare and misalignment checks in decode, then emit the early redirect information.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Remove branch compare work from the hot EX cone and keep JALR plus non-branch ALU work on the live execute path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Rewire redirect control so the ID-stage branch resolver can drive fetch without waiting for EX on B-type branches.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-t