{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778871558215,"sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2fdeffeQAYXcs2lbR0wva","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_87QqYNjAizIhV34qnKqL7poT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"structural|pipeline|fetch|forward|branch|BTB|cache","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 13 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 2: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Retime control-flow arithmetic\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move common control-flow arithmetic earlier in the pipe: carry a precomputed PC+4 value forward from fetch, precompute branch and JALR targets in decode, and let EX only perform the branch compare plus a small target select. This should shorten the EX critical path and raise clock speed without changing retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside decode and latch them into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed targets and remove target adders from the EX critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside d...\n  Line 3: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Retime branch target generation\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes the taken-branch redirect path and feeds it\\nstraight back into the PC update logic in the same cycle. That creates a\\nwide EX-to-IF feedback cone that is a natural Fmax limiter on this small\\nin-order core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes the taken-branch redirect path and feeds it\\nstraight back into the PC update logic in the same cycle. That creates a\\nwide EX-to-IF feedback cone that is a natural Fmax limiter on this small\\nin-order core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute the branch/JAL target in ID, carry it as a registered sideband\\nthrough the pipeline, and let EX use that latched target instead of\\nrecomputing pc+imm on the critical redirect path. This should shorten the\\nbranch feedback cone without changing branch penalties or architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a decoded branch-target sideband to the ID/EX bundle so it can be carried forward as a registered value.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc+imm for branch/JAL instructions during decode, alongside the existing control signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched target for branch/JAL redirects and keep only the JALR adder on the live EX critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a decoded branch-target sideband to the ID/EX bundle so it can be carried forward as a registered value.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc+imm for branch/JAL instructions during decode, alongside the existing control signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched target for branch/JAL redirects and keep...\n  Line 4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Backward branch taken predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops, and this baseline core still\\nfetches pc+4 until EX resolves every branch. That means each taken backward\\nloop branch pays a fixed wrong-path flush even though the direction is\\nobvious from the branch immediate sign bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops, and this baseline core still\\nfetches pc+4 until EX resolves every branch. That means each taken backward\\nloop branch pays a fixed wrong-path flush even though the direction is\\nobvious from the branch immediate sign bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny static predictor in IF that recognizes legal B-type branches and\\npredicts backward branches taken when the branch immediate is negative.\\nRecompute the same prediction in EX so correctly predicted branches do not\\nredirect, and only mispredictions flush the frontend. Keep JAL/JALR as EX-\\nresolved control flow to avoid introducing a BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add static backward-branch prediction in fetch and choose the predicted next PC before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual branch outcome against the IF prediction and redirect only on mispredict.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add static backward-branch prediction in fetch and choose the predicted next PC before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual branch outcome against the IF prediction and redirect only on mispredict.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 306.86, \"delta_pct\": 8.5, \"vs_baseline\": 8.5, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.24, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\"...\n  Line 6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"(slot 1 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent did not write a file for slot hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (allowed_yaml_ids=['hyp-20260515-001-r2s0', 'hyp-20260515-002-r2s1', 'hyp-20260515-003-r2s2'])\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2}\n\n  Line 8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Gate dead forwarding compares\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Thread the decoded control bundle into the forwarding logic and short-circuit\\nequality compares for source operands the instruction cannot actually use.\\nInstructions like OP-IMM, loads, JAL, LUI, and AUIPC should skip the dead\\ncompare path entirely while preserving the existing forwarding priority when\\na source is live. This should trim the common EX cone without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 327.95, \"delta_pct\": -2.31...\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass selection into ID, latch already-forwarded\\nrs1/rs2 values in the ID/EX register, and let EX consume stable operands\\ndirectly. Keep the existing load-use stall rule and x0 filtering intact so\\ncorrectness stays the same while the EX combinational cone gets shorter.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwarding before the ID/EX flop and latch the selected operands into the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume pre-forwarded operands directly and drop the operand-select muxes from the EX critical path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retime or simplify bypass selection so it serves the ID-side operand latch instead of EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwardin...\n  Line 10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark loops revisit the same taken branches many times, but this core\\nstill fetches sequentially until EX resolves control flow. A tiny target\\ncache can turn repeated loop branches into predicted fetches and trim the\\nrecurring wrong-path flush cost without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark loops revisit the same taken branches many times, but this core\\nstill fetches sequentially until EX resolves control flow. A tiny target\\ncache can turn repeated loop branches into predicted fetches and trim the\\nrecurring wrong-path flush cost without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer in IF that stores the\\nPC tag and resolved target for taken B-type branches and JALs. On a BTB\\nhit, fetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through as usual.\\nUpdate the entry from the existing EX redirect path so the predictor uses\\ncached targets instead of re-decoding branch immediates in fetch.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add BTB lookup/predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the BTB from resolved taken branches and JAL redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add any small predictor-sideband fields needed to carry BTB state cleanly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add BTB lookup/predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the BTB from resolved taken branches and JAL redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add any small predictor-sideband fields needed to carry BTB state cleanly.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_p...\n  Line 11: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Retime load/store lane metadata\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\\nextraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\\nloads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\\nraise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current MEM stage computes byte masks, alignment, and load-data\\nextraction in one combinational block. CoreMark exercises a lot of simple\\nloads and stores, so shrinking that memory-side cone is a plausible way to\\nraise Fmax without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute and carry the load/store lane metadata out of EX: word-aligned\\naddress, byte mask, and byte-lane shift/selection can be latched with the\\nEX/MEM payload so MEM only has to perform the actual memory access and a\\nmuch smaller extract/extend step. This should reduce the hot memory-path\\nlogic seen by synthesis while preserving retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the lane metadata once the ALU result is known so the memory stage no longer needs to decode width/address details.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried metadata to simplify byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic on the MEM critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM and MEM/WB sideband fields for predecoded load/store lane metadata and aligned address handling.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the lane metadata once the ALU result is known so the memory stage no longer needs ...\n  Line 12: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r4s1\", \"title\": \"Split divide from ALU\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps the full RV32M divide/remainder logic in the common\\ncombinational datapath. That is expensive logic on a small FPGA, even though\\nCoreMark is much more branch- and multiply-heavy than divide-heavy. Removing\\nDIV/REM from the hot ALU cone should raise Fmax without changing the ISA-\\nvisible result stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current ALU keeps the full RV32M divide/remainder logic in the common\\ncombinational datapath. That is expensive logic on a small FPGA, even though\\nCoreMark is much more branch- and multiply-heavy than divide-heavy. Removing\\nDIV/REM from the hot ALU cone should raise Fmax without changing the ISA-\\nvisible result stream.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Keep the one-cycle ALU for ADD/SUB/logic/shifts and the multiply ops, but\\nmove DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a small iterative side unit that only stalls the\\npipe when a divide is actually executing. Expose the divide result back\\nthrough the existing EX/WB retirement path and preserve the RV32M corner\\ncases exactly. This is a pure structural split that should shrink the common\\ncritical path while leaving non-divide CoreMark code on the fast path.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the divider/remainder combinational cone from the common ALU path and keep the fast integer/multiply ops single-cycle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/div_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a small iterative divider/remainder engine that returns RV32M-correct results and handles divide-by-zero and overflow cases.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Route DIV/REM instructions into the divider unit and hold the EX/MEM state until the result is ready.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Treat an active divide as a pipeline stall source so younger instructions do not advance while the divider r...\n  Line 13: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Single-entry loop target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps hitting the same inner-loop branch, but this core still\\nwaits for EX to resolve control flow before it can reuse a taken target.\\nA predictor that remembers just the hottest resolved transfer can cut\\nrepeated wrong-path fetches without pulling a general BTB or history RAM\\ninto the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a single-entry hot-branch predictor in IF that stores one recently\\nresolved taken B-type/JAL PC, its target, and a valid bit. On a PC match,\\nfetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through and let the\\nexisting EX redirect train the entry from the resolved path. Keep JALR and\\nlegality checks off the predictor fast path so the hardware stays small\\nenough for Tang Nano 20K and the formal state stays bounded.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved PC metadata into IF so the single-entry predictor can train on redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the one-entry predictor lookup/update logic and use it to select the next fetch PC.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 335.7, \"delta_pct...\n  Line 14: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r5s0\", \"title\": \"Predecode hot instruction fields\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current decode path fans the full 32-bit instruction into legality,\\nregister address extraction, and hazard checks. On a small FPGA, that\\nrepeated slicing and nested opcode logic is a plausible Fmax limiter once\\nthe branch-target cone has already been trimmed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current decode path fans the full 32-bit instruction into legality,\\nregister address extraction, and hazard checks. On a small FPGA, that\\nrepeated slicing and nested opcode logic is a plausible Fmax limiter once\\nthe branch-target cone has already been trimmed.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move instruction-field extraction to the IF/ID boundary: latch opcode,\\nfunct3, funct7, rd, rs1, rs2, and EBREAK qualification in the pipeline\\nbundle, then have `decoder` and `hazard_unit` consume those predecoded\\nfields instead of re-slicing the raw instruction word. This should cut\\ndecode fanout and simplify the common ID critical path without changing\\nISA-visible behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predecoded IF/ID sideband fields for opcode/funct/register-address metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Extract and latch the instruction metadata once when fetching, including EBREAK qualification.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/decoder.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the narrower predecoded fields instead of repeatedly slicing the raw instruction bus.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the latched source register addresses from IF/ID so load-use checks stop fanning out the full instruction word.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the new predecoded bundle through decode and keep the ID/EX register semantics unchanged.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg....\n  Line 15: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r5s1\", \"title\": \"Early branch resolution\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage still carries branch compare, redirect selection, and the\\nforwarding muxes on the same path. CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight\\nloops, so taking conditional branches off that cone should help both Fmax\\nand the loop-throughput side of the fitness score.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage still carries branch compare, redirect selection, and the\\nforwarding muxes on the same path. CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight\\nloops, so taking conditional branches off that cone should help both Fmax\\nand the loop-throughput side of the fitness score.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move B-type branch resolution into ID so BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU can\\nredirect one stage earlier, while leaving JALR in EX to preserve the\\nfreshness guarantees on rs1. The common case then stops paying branch\\ncompare cost in EX, and the hot redirect path becomes shorter without\\nchanging architectural results.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retarget operand selection so ID can see fresher rs1/rs2 values for conditional branch compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve conditional branch compare and misalignment checks in decode, then emit the early redirect information.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove branch compare work from the hot EX cone and keep JALR plus non-branch ALU work on the live execute path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Rewire redirect control so the ID-stage branch resolver can drive fetch without waiting for EX on B-type branches.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retarget operand selection so ID can see fresher rs1/rs2 values for conditional branch compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"descri...\n  Line 16: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r5s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny return-address stack\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark and its library calls spend meaningful time in call/return\\ntraffic, and this core still resolves every JALR return after fetch.\\nA bounded return predictor can cut those recurring wrong-path flushes\\nwithout dragging a general BTB or branch-immediate decode into IF.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark and its library calls spend meaningful time in call/return\\ntraffic, and this core still resolves every JALR return after fetch.\\nA bounded return predictor can cut those recurring wrong-path flushes\\nwithout dragging a general BTB or branch-immediate decode into IF.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small return-address stack that predicts JALR returns from\\nthe common link-register pattern and trains only on resolved JAL/JALR\\ncontrol flow. Keep the predictor state bounded and the fetch-side check\\nsimple, so IF uses only opcode/rd/rs1 bits already present in the fetched\\ninstruction while EX remains the source of truth for updates and\\nmispredict recovery.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack and use it to choose the predicted next PC for return-like JALR fetches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate predictor update metadata from resolved JAL/JALR control flow and redirect on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the predictor update signals between EX and IF without changing the RVFI or memory IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a tiny return-address stack and use it to choose the predicted next PC for return-like JALR fetches.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate predictor update metadata from resolved JAL/JALR control flow and redirect on mispredict...","metadata":{"matches":13,"truncated":false},"title":"structural|pipeline|fetch|forward|branch|BTB|cache","time":{"start":1778871558209,"end":1778871558214}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0f353ef3da99f3d3016a076d06171c81989e65abff84150060"}},"id":"prt_e2d01e03f001FWIXPPLc37LzmJ","sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2fdeffeQAYXcs2lbR0wva","messageID":"msg_e2d01d07d001SD85gYmZdLskyt"}}
