{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778871572090,"sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2fdeffeQAYXcs2lbR0wva","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_WT7GpqktlO5DOlfBksjLDKHS","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"hyp-20260515-001-r4s0|hyp-20260515-002-r4s1|hyp-20260515-001-r3s0|hyp-20260515-002-r3s1","path":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","include":"*.jsonl"},"output":"Found 4 matches\n/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:\n  Line 8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Gate dead forwarding compares\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Thread the decoded control bundle into the forwarding logic and short-circuit\\nequality compares for source operands the instruction cannot actually use.\\nInstructions like OP-IMM, loads, JAL, LUI, and AUIPC should skip the dead\\ncompare path entirely while preserving the existing forwarding priority when\\na source is live. This should trim the common EX cone without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 327.95, \"delta_pct\": -2.31...\n  Line 9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass selection into ID, latch already-forwarded\\nrs1/rs2 values in the ID/EX register, and let EX consume stable operands\\ndirectly. Keep the existing load-use stall rule and x0 filtering intact so\\ncorrectness stays the same while the EX combinational cone gets shorter.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from t