/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside decode and latch them into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed targets and remove target adders from the EX critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside d...\n  Line 3: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Retime branch target generation\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes the taken-branch redirect path and feeds it\\nstraight back into the PC update logic in the same cycle. That creates a\\nwide EX-to-IF feedback cone that is a natural Fmax limiter on this small\\nin-order core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes the taken-branch redirect path and feeds it\\nstraight back into the PC update logic in the same cycle. That creates a\\nwide EX-to-IF feedback cone that is a natural Fmax limiter on this small\\nin-order core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute the branch/JAL target in ID, carry it as a registered sideband\\nthrough the pipeline, and let EX use that latched target instead of\\nrecomputing pc+imm on the critical redirect path. This should shorten the\\nbranch feedback cone without changing branch penalties or architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a decoded branch-target sideband to the ID/EX bundle so it can be carried forward as a registered value.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\":