{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778872798271,"sessionID":"ses_1d2ebb45dffevVAv65hGsXg646","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_XfkOhImyexpGfmlWDVH5W8tU","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r7s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r7s1\n+title: \"Split retire snapshot\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current MEM/WB bundle carries both writeback state and a large set of\n+  RVFI-only retire fields through the hottest part of the pipeline. That wide\n+  payload increases routing and fanout even though most of it is only needed at\n+  commit time.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Split the retirement metadata from the live writeback path: keep a narrow\n+  MEM/WB register for regfile writeback and forwarding, and capture the RVFI\n+  fields into a separate commit snapshot at the retirement boundary. This should\n+  reduce the width and fanout of the common MEM/WB/WB cone while preserving the\n+  architectural stream and all RVFI semantics.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Define a slimmer live writeback bundle plus a separate retire-snapshot type for RVFI-only metadata.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Populate the narrow writeback state and a separate retirement snapshot instead of carrying one wide shared bundle.\"\n+  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Consume only the narrow writeback bundle for regfile updates so the fast path no longer drags RVFI fields.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Wire the retire snapshot to the RVFI outputs while keeping the execution/writeback pipeline semantics unchanged.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r7s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/