{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778873945730,"sessionID":"ses_1d2daeaf6ffeouNJg2hv08IAP2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_l2MZpr4iiHY23L2nUkaRtpjW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r8s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r8s1\n+title: \"ID branch resolve\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops, so conditional branch\n+  redirects are on a hot path even in a simple in-order core. Moving the\n+  B-type compare and redirect decision earlier should shorten the common\n+  execute cone and reduce the cost of taken loop branches.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Resolve B-type branches in ID using the already-decoded branch target and\n+  forwarded source operands, while leaving JALR and all non-branch ALU work\n+  in EX. This should remove branch compare and redirect selection from the\n+  hot EX path without changing architectural results or the load-use stall\n+  discipline.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add a compact branch-resolve sideband so the ID-stage decision can flow through the pipeline cleanly.\"\n+  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Retarget operand selection so ID can obtain fresh rs1/rs2 values for conditional branch compares.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Compare B-type branches in decode, latch the taken decision and redirect target, and emit the early redirect info.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Remove conditional branch compare work from EX and keep JALR plus ordinary ALU work on the live execute path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Merge the ID-stage branch redirect with the existing control-flow path while preserving the RVFI and memory contract.\"\n