{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778875391061,"sessionID":"ses_1d2c529e4ffeL1EhVDvP24MXrc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_swc3RAfQru101YTOAHFxx2St","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r9s1.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-002-r9s1\n+title: \"Split RV32M from ALU\"\n+category: structural\n+motivation: |\n+  The current ALU computes RV32M products and quotients inside the same\n+  combinational block as ADD/SUB/logic/shift work. That makes the execute\n+  path wider than it needs to be, even on instructions that never use the\n+  M-extension.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Move MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU/DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU into a dedicated RV32M side\n+  unit so the common integer ALU only carries RV32I operations. Keep the\n+  multiply path single-cycle if the FPGA maps it well, and let DIV/REM use a\n+  small stalled engine; this should shrink the hot EX cone without changing\n+  architectural results.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n+    description: \"Remove RV32M execution from the common ALU datapath and keep the module focused on RV32I arithmetic and logic.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Route M-extension ops into the dedicated side unit and preserve the existing retirement/writeback behavior.\"\n+  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Treat a busy divide path as a stall source so the pipe only waits when the side unit is actually occupied.\"\n+  - file: rtl/mul_div_unit.sv\n+    description: \"Add the dedicated RV32M execution unit with correct multiply and divide/remainder corner cases.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-002-r9s1.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-2