{"type":"text","timestamp":1778876787249,"sessionID":"ses_1d2af83a7ffeN3uktonXlDjd6a","part":{"id":"prt_e2d51a9eb001Ne6J3x03SaABHq","messageID":"msg_e2d515e55001fnrYVqMLvqaQiH","sessionID":"ses_1d2af83a7ffeN3uktonXlDjd6a","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis file now. The angle is a smaller predictor state footprint, not a bigger BTB, so it should avoid the fetch-path bloat that hurt the earlier attempts.","time":{"start":1778876787179,"end":1778876787249},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0614c9d2810ec8e2016a0781730e74819aa6bc255fbd6981ed","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778876788215,"sessionID":"ses_1d2af83a7ffeN3uktonXlDjd6a","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_8kvxVqWpdebepRctAmqaHN2i","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r10s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r10s2\n+title: \"Short backedge delta predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still spends a lot of time in short inner loops, but the core\n+  fetches sequentially until EX resolves each taken backedge. Prior predictor\n+  attempts were too general and widened the fetch cone; a smaller, loop-only\n+  predictor with a compact state footprint could recover the recurring flush\n+  cost without dragging a full BTB or return stack into IF.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a tiny exact-match predictor for short taken backward B-type branches\n+  only. Train it from resolved EX redirects, but store a compact signed delta\n+  rather than a full target so the fetch-side datapath stays narrow; if the\n+  branch offset does not fit the compressed form, fall back to the existing\n+  EX-resolved path. Keep JAL/JALR and forward branches off the predictor fast\n+  path so the hardware remains bounded and formal stays tractable.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add the short-backedge lookup, compressed delta storage, and predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Emit the resolved branch metadata needed to train or invalidate the predictor on taken backedges and mispredicts.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the predictor update path between EX and IF without changing the RVFI or memory IO contract.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r10s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/b