{"type":"text","timestamp":1778878084707,"sessionID":"ses_1d29c3c44ffeoVv6yatgSXHaLk","part":{"id":"prt_e2d65765d001u3S8uGu29L9wGB","messageID":"msg_e2d649233001VIAMP8WXyjBJrZ","sessionID":"ses_1d29c3c44ffeoVv6yatgSXHaLk","type":"text","text":"I’ve narrowed it to a very small unconditional-call predictor: only `JAL`, no BTB/RAS/history, and with the prediction carried as a sideband so EX can suppress redundant redirects when it matches. Writing that hypothesis now.","time":{"start":1778878084701,"end":1778878084704},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_07f6e4021cd90a36016a0786845c2c819988354b7a252d070a","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778878085591,"sessionID":"ses_1d29c3c44ffeoVv6yatgSXHaLk","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_JJaf5zGqECCCr692b2Gi8mJE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r11s2\n+title: \"JAL fast-path predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Prior predictor attempts added too much fetch-side state or compare logic and\n+  lost more Fmax than they saved in flushes. CoreMark still pays a full EX-\n+  resolved redirect on every JAL call, so a narrower unconditional predictor\n+  may recover some of that control-flow cost without dragging in BTB or RAS\n+  machinery.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Predict unconditional JALs in IF by decoding only the JAL opcode and\n+  computing the J-type target on the fetch side. Carry the predicted next PC\n+  alongside the instruction so EX can suppress the redundant redirect when the\n+  target matches, leaving JALR and conditional branches on the existing path.\n+  This targets call traffic with far less state than the failed BTB/RAS style\n+  predictors.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: low\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact prediction sideband fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so fetch can carry a predicted next PC forward.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Recognize JAL in fetch, compute its target immediately, and mark the prediction as valid for the downstream stages.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the prediction sideband with the decoded instruction so EX can compare the predicted and resolved next PCs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Suppress the redundant redirect on correctly predicted JALs while keeping JALR and branch resolution unchanged.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r11s2\n+title: \"JAL fast-path predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Prior predictor attempts added too much fetch-side state or compare logic and\n+  lost more Fmax than they saved in flushes. CoreMark still pays a full EX-\n+  resolved redirect on every JAL call, so a narrower unconditional predictor\n+  may recover some of that control-flow cost without dragging in BTB or RAS\n+  machinery.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Predict unconditional JALs in IF by decoding only the JAL opcode and\n+  computing the J-type target on the fetch side. Carry the predicted next PC\n+  alongside the instruction so EX can suppress the redundant redirect when the\n+  target matches, leaving JALR and conditional branches on the existing path.\n+  This targets call traffic with far less state than the failed BTB/RAS style\n+  predictors.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: low\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact prediction sideband fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so fetch can carry a predicted next PC forward.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Recognize JAL in fetch, compute its target immediately, and mark the prediction as valid for the downstream stages.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the prediction sideband with the decoded instruction so EX can compare the predicted and resolved next PCs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Suppress the redundant redirect on correctly predicted JALs while keeping JALR and branch resolution unchanged.\"\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml","relativePath":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\n+++ /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml\n@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r11s2\n+title: \"JAL fast-path predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  Prior predictor attempts added too much fetch-side state or compare logic and\n+  lost more Fmax than they saved in flushes. CoreMark still pays a full EX-\n+  resolved redirect on every JAL call, so a narrower unconditional predictor\n+  may recover some of that control-flow cost without dragging in BTB or RAS\n+  machinery.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Predict unconditional JALs in IF by decoding only the JAL opcode and\n+  computing the J-type target on the fetch side. Carry the predicted next PC\n+  alongside the instruction so EX can suppress the redundant redirect when the\n+  target matches, leaving JALR and conditional branches on the existing path.\n+  This targets call traffic with far less state than the failed BTB/RAS style\n+  predictors.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: low\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add compact prediction sideband fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so fetch can carry a predicted next PC forward.\"\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Recognize JAL in fetch, compute its target immediately, and mark the prediction as valid for the downstream stages.\"\n+  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Latch the prediction sideband with the decoded instruction so EX can compare the predicted and resolved next PCs.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Suppress the redundant redirect on correctly predicted JALs while keeping JALR and branch resolution unchanged.\"\n","additions":28,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r11s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778878085582,"end":1778878085589}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07f6e4021cd90a36016a07868478348199915d30d434425103"}},"id":"prt_e2d6576610019DmL1gYjwtcHUm","sessionID":"ses_1d29c3c44ffeoVv6yatgSXHaLk","messageID":"msg_e2d649233001VIAMP8WXyjBJrZ"}}
