e combinational branches so each op type only carries the logic it actually needs.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Separate the load and store combinational branches so each op type only carries the logic it actually needs.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 328.78, \"delta_pct\": -3.19, \"vs_baseline\": 16.25, \"fmax_mhz\": 147.67, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9818, \"ff\": 1960, \"seeds\": [150.99, 147.67, 133.71], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T20:33:43.049217Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 10, \"scribe_skipped\": \"PermissionError: scribe touched off-limits paths and was rolled back: ['cores/bench/rtl/core.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'cor...\n  Line 30: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed fetch boundary\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The remaining hot path is likely the combinational fetch-to-decode loop,\\nwhere `imem_data` still fans into decode, hazard checks, and PC control in\\nthe same cycle. Breaking that boundary should give synthesis a cleaner\\nstage cut than another fetch-side predictor, especially after the branch\\ntarget work already moved earlier.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The remaining hot path is likely the combinational fetch-to-decode loop,\\nwhere `imem_data` still fans into decode, hazard checks, and PC control in\\nthe same cycle. Breaking that boundary should give synthesis a cleaner\\nstage cut than another fetch-side predictor, especially after the branch\\ntarget work already moved earlier.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Insert a real IF/ID register so fetched instructions are latched once\\nbefore decode and hazard logic see them. That should shorten the\\nimem-to-decode-to-flush