{"type":"text","timestamp":1778879176008,"sessionID":"ses_1d28b9135ffe7A36ywoiVX75Fk","part":{"id":"prt_e2d761cb8001i5O2IvmlVAmvsS","messageID":"msg_e2d75d341001t4k7YebSFwTi7O","sessionID":"ses_1d28b9135ffe7A36ywoiVX75Fk","type":"text","text":"I’m writing the hypothesis now. It stays narrow: canonical call/return only, no general BTB, no extra branch decode beyond what fetch already sees.","time":{"start":1778879175864,"end":1778879176007},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_05b587378a5d322b016a078ac77e28819ab189528deb9fe08d","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778879177559,"sessionID":"ses_1d28b9135ffe7A36ywoiVX75Fk","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_hyA1oWws5kUOFILuLgfIiigh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r12s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r12s2\n+title: \"Canonical return stack\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark still spends real time in call/return traffic, but the core only\n+  fast-paths unconditional JAL today. A tiny return predictor can remove the\n+  recurring JALR redirections from library calls without pulling a general BTB\n+  or wider branch history into the fetch cone.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a two-entry return-address stack that trains only on canonical calls\n+  using x1/x5 link registers and predicts only canonical return JALR patterns\n+  (rs1 = x1/x5, imm = 0, rd = x0). Keep conditional branches and non-return\n+  JALR on the existing EX-resolved path, and reuse the existing predicted-next-\n+  PC sideband so IF can select the return target without adding a general target\n+  cache. This should trim CoreMark's call/return flushes while keeping the\n+  predictor state tiny and bounded.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 4\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add the small return-stack lookup in fetch and use it to choose the next PC for canonical return-like JALR instructions.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Generate return-stack push/pop update signals from resolved JAL and JALR control flow, and redirect on return mispredicts.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the predictor update metadata between EX and IF without changing the RVFI or memory IO contract.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/