ion payload to `RESET_PC` and `NOP`, even though those fields are\\nconsumed only when `replay_cand_valid_q` is asserted and the existing full-PC\\nguard matches the current fetch PC. Reset muxes and reset fanout on these\\n64 payload bits sit next to the IF replay/fetch-ready path that now matters\\nmost for Fmax. Clearing only the candidate valid bit should preserve the\\ncurrent replay hit rate and all visible behavior while trimming a small but\\ntiming-relevant reset structure.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current best result is built around the registered lookahead instruction\\nreplay predictor. The strongest recent micro-opt win came from compressing\\nreplay tags and making replay table payload arrays resetless behind valid\\nbits; broader attempts to remove the replay candidate PC guard or apply\\nvalid-only reset discipline across the whole pipeline regressed. That points\\nto a narrower follow-up in the same proven area.\\n\\n`if_stage` still synchronously resets the registered replay candidate PC and\\ninstruction payload to `RESET_PC` and `NOP`, even though those fields are\\nconsumed only when `replay_cand_valid_q` is asserted and the existing full-PC\\nguard matches the current fetch PC. Reset muxes and reset fanout on these\\n64 payload bits sit next to the IF replay/fetch-ready path that now matters\\nmost for Fmax. Clearing only ...\n  Line 48: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260428-041-r16s1\", \"title\": \"Same-Cycle Store Slot Refill\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current best core already has the two structural wins that matter most:\\nregistered instruction replay hides many random iStall cycles, and the\\none-deep pending-store slot lets a stalled normal-RAM store retire before\\nthe external dmem write is accepted. The remaining store-side bottleneck is\\nnarrower than a full second buffer entry. When the pending slot is valid, the\\nMEM stage currently treats every younger memory operation as blocked even on\\nthe 