{"type":"text","timestamp":1778839589295,"sessionID":"ses_1d4e69b92ffe5Xxm2MpEuAdKx0","part":{"id":"prt_e2b1a10fd001d04yYMRhck82HJ","messageID":"msg_e2b1975ec001kVBYxYdhRxVRTC","sessionID":"ses_1d4e69b92ffe5Xxm2MpEuAdKx0","type":"text","text":"The prior static predictor lost because it put branch-immediate work on the IF path. I’m targeting a BTB-backed predictor instead: reuse a cached target in fetch, update it in EX, and avoid recomputing immediates in the hot front-end cone.","time":{"start":1778839589117,"end":1778839589277},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_09f654b9fbdde48f016a06f024db308198968b4eded1ab9b6d","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778839589340,"sessionID":"ses_1d4e69b92ffe5Xxm2MpEuAdKx0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_YIbZwaAYzSOjhGz7Kb21A0Qz","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","offset":1,"limit":8},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"id\": \"baseline-bench-07fd61d\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T09:45:09.943336Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Retime control-flow arithmetic\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move common control-flow arithmetic earlier in the pipe: carry a precomputed PC+4 value forward from fetch, precompute branch and JALR targets in decode, and let EX only perform the branch compare plus a small target select. This should shorten the EX critical path and raise clock speed without changing retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside decode and latch them into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed targets and remove target adders from the EX critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside d... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Retime branch target generation\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes the taken-branch redirect path and feeds it\\nstraight back into the PC update logic in the same cycle. That creates a\\nwide EX-to-IF feedback cone that is a natural Fmax limiter on this small\\nin-order core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage computes the taken-branch redirect path and feeds it\\nstraight back into the PC update logic in the same cycle. That creates a\\nwide EX-to-IF feedback cone that is a natural Fmax limiter on this small\\nin-order core.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Precompute the branch/JAL target in ID, carry it as a registered sideband\\nthrough the pipeline, and let EX use that latched target instead of\\nrecomputing pc+imm on the critical redirect path. This should shorten the\\nbranch feedback cone without changing branch penalties or architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a decoded branch-target sideband to the ID/EX bundle so it can be carried forward as a registered value.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc+imm for branch/JAL instructions during decode, alongside the existing control signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched target for branch/JAL redirects and keep only the JALR adder on the live EX critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a decoded branch-target sideband to the ID/EX bundle so it can be carried forward as a registered value.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch pc+imm for branch/JAL instructions during decode, alongside the existing control signals.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the latched target for branch/JAL redirects and keep... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n4: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Backward branch taken predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops, and this baseline core still\\nfetches pc+4 until EX resolves every branch. That means each taken backward\\nloop branch pays a fixed wrong-path flush even though the direction is\\nobvious from the branch immediate sign bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops, and this baseline core still\\nfetches pc+4 until EX resolves every branch. That means each taken backward\\nloop branch pays a fixed wrong-path flush even though the direction is\\nobvious from the branch immediate sign bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny static predictor in IF that recognizes legal B-type branches and\\npredicts backward branches taken when the branch immediate is negative.\\nRecompute the same prediction in EX so correctly predicted branches do not\\nredirect, and only mispredictions flush the frontend. Keep JAL/JALR as EX-\\nresolved control flow to avoid introducing a BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add static backward-branch prediction in fetch and choose the predicted next PC before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual branch outcome against the IF prediction and redirect only on mispredict.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add static backward-branch prediction in fetch and choose the predicted next PC before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual branch outcome against the IF prediction and redirect only on mispredict.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 306.86, \"delta_pct\": 8.5, \"vs_baseline\": 8.5, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.24, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 4 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-07fd61d\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null,