{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778854648259,"sessionID":"ses_1d401591bffeuKVrVJzOl0LPN4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_i3jIyp2bqpEaYm9mjU1lltFf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r3s2\n+title: \"Tiny BTB target cache\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark loops revisit the same taken branches many times, but this core\n+  still fetches sequentially until EX resolves control flow. A tiny target\n+  cache can turn repeated loop branches into predicted fetches and trim the\n+  recurring wrong-path flush cost without changing architectural behavior.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer in IF that stores the\n+  PC tag and resolved target for taken B-type branches and JALs. On a BTB\n+  hit, fetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through as usual.\n+  Update the entry from the existing EX redirect path so the predictor uses\n+  cached targets instead of re-decoding branch immediates in fetch.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add BTB lookup/predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train the BTB from resolved taken branches and JAL redirects.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n+    description: \"Add any small predictor-sideband fields needed to carry BTB state cleanly.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r3s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-re