even though the direction is\\nobvious from the branch immediate sign bit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny static predictor in IF that recognizes legal B-type branches and\\npredicts backward branches taken when the branch immediate is negative.\\nRecompute the same prediction in EX so correctly predicted branches do not\\nredirect, and only mispredictions flush the frontend. Keep JAL/JALR as EX-\\nresolved control flow to avoid introducing a BTB or return stack.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add static backward-branch prediction in fetch and choose the predicted next PC before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual branch outcome against the IF prediction and redirect only on mispredict.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add static backward-branch prediction in fetch and choose the predicted next PC before EX resolves the branch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare actual branch outcome against the IF prediction and redirect only on mispredict.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 306.86, \"delta_pct\": 8.5, \"vs_baseline\": 8.5, \"fmax_mhz\": 132.24, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4309463, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\"... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n5: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"(slot 0 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent did not write a file for slot hyp-20260515-001-r2s0 (allowed_yaml_ids=['hyp-20260515-001-r2s0', 'hyp-20260515-002-r2s1', 'hyp-20260515-003-r2s2'])\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 2}\n6: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"(slot 1 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent did not write a file for slot hyp-20260515-002-r2s1 (allowed_yaml_ids=['hyp-20260515-001-r2s0', 'hyp-20260515-002-r2s1', 'hyp-20260515-003-r2s2'])\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 2}\n7: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"(slot 2 hypothesis-gen failed)\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_passed\": false, \"error\": \"hypothesis_gen_failed: Hypothesis agent did not write a file for slot hyp-20260515-003-r2s2 (allowed_yaml_ids=['hyp-20260515-001-r2s0', 'hyp-20260515-002-r2s1', 'hyp-20260515-003-r2s2'])\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2}\n8: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Gate dead forwarding compares\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time on simple ALU and load instructions that only\\nread one source register. The current forwarding logic still evaluates both\\nrs1 and rs2 compare trees on every cycle, which adds unnecessary fanout to\\nthe EX input path on a small FPGA.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Thread the decoded control bundle into the forwarding logic and short-circuit\\nequality compares for source operands the instruction cannot actually use.\\nInstructions like OP-IMM, loads, JAL, LUI, and AUIPC should skip the dead\\ncompare path entirely while preserving the existing forwarding priority when\\na source is live. This should trim the common EX cone without changing ISA\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Pass the decoded control bundle into the forwarding unit so operand-use gating is available on the EX path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Skip rs1/rs2 equality chains for instructions that do not consume that source operand, while keeping the same priority when they do.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 327.95, \"delta_pct\": -2.31... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n9: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r3s1\", \"title\": \"Retimed operand bypass\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage still pays for operand bypass selection on every\\ninstruction, even when the result is just a simple ALU op or a branch\\ncompare. Moving that muxing work earlier is a clean structural way to\\nshrink the common critical path without changing ISA behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass selection into ID, latch already-forwarded\\nrs1/rs2 values in the ID/EX register, and let EX consume stable operands\\ndirectly. Keep the existing load-use stall rule and x0 filtering intact so\\ncorrectness stays the same while the EX combinational cone gets shorter.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwarding before the ID/EX flop and latch the selected operands into the pipeline register.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume pre-forwarded operands directly and drop the operand-select muxes from the EX critical path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retime or simplify bypass selection so it serves the ID-side operand latch instead of EX.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the bypass-source values into ID and remove the EX-stage forwarding plumbing from the top-level wiring.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Resolve rs1/rs2 forwardin... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n10: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Tiny BTB target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark loops revisit the same taken branches many times, but this core\\nstill fetches sequentially until EX resolves control flow. A tiny target\\ncache can turn repeated loop branches into predicted fetches and trim the\\nrecurring wrong-path flush cost without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark loops revisit the same taken branches many times, but this core\\nstill fetches sequentially until EX resolves control flow. A tiny target\\ncache can turn repeated loop branches into predicted fetches and trim the\\nrecurring wrong-path flush cost without changing architectural behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a very small direct-mapped branch target buffer in IF that stores the\\nPC tag and resolved target for taken B-type branches and JALs. On a BTB\\nhit, fetch the cached target immediately; otherwise fall through as usual.\\nUpdate the entry from the existing EX redirect path so the predictor uses\\ncached targets instead of re-decoding branch immediates in fetch.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add BTB lookup/predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the BTB from resolved taken branches and JAL redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add any small predictor-sideband fields needed to carry BTB state cleanly.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add BTB lookup/predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the BTB from resolved taken branches and JAL redirects.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add any small predictor-sideband fields needed to carry BTB state cleanly.\"}], \"outcome\": \"broken\", \"formal_passed\": false, \"cosim_p... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 10 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-07fd61d\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 282.82, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 127.03, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9563, \"ff\": 1866, \"seeds\": [128.72, 127.03, 123.02], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T09:45:09.943336Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Retime control-flow arithmetic\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current EX stage recomputes PC-relative and jump-target arithmetic on the same path as branch compare and redirect selection. On a small FPGA like Tang Nano 20K, that wide combinational path is a likely Fmax limiter even when the ISA behavior is already correct.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move common control-flow arithmetic earlier in the pipe: carry a precomputed PC+4 value forward from fetch, precompute branch and JALR targets in decode, and let EX only perform the branch compare plus a small target select. This should shorten the EX critical path and raise clock speed without changing retirement semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside decode and latch them into ID/EX.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the precomputed targets and remove target adders from the EX critical path.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add pipeline-bundle fields for precomputed PC+4 and control-flow targets.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Forward the fetch PC+4 value so EX no longer recomputes it.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Precompute branch and JALR targets alongside d... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r1s1\