{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778871625115,"sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2f76ffeLmDxOQPnceYbHn","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PCcqOb6DN13kygUOtBnPjiSh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r6s0.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r6s0.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-001-r6s0\n2: title: \"Retimed memory lane metadata\"\n3: category: micro_opt\n4: motivation: |\n5:   The MEM stage still recomputes byte masks, alignment, and load extraction\n6:   from the full ALU result on every load/store. On a small FPGA, that keeps\n7:   a fairly wide combinational cone on the memory side of the pipe.\n8: hypothesis: |\n9:   Precompute the load/store lane metadata in EX and carry it through the\n10:   EX/MEM payload so MEM only performs the actual bus access plus a much\n11:   smaller extract/extend step. This should trim the common memory-path logic\n12:   without changing retirement semantics or ISA-visible behavior.\n13: expected_impact:\n14:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n15:   confidence: medium\n16: changes:\n17:   - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n18:     description: \"Add EX/MEM sideband fields for predecoded lane metadata such as alignment, mask, and shift information.\"\n19:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n20:     description: \"Compute and latch the memory lane metadata once the effective address is known, instead of re-deriving it in MEM.\"\n21:   - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n22:     description: \"Consume the carried metadata so byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic no longer dominate the MEM cone.\"\n\n(End of file - total 22 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Retimed memory lane metadata\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The MEM stage still recomputes byte masks, alignment, and load extraction\n  from the full ALU result on every load/store. On a small FPGA, that keeps\n  a fairly wide combinational cone on the memory side of the pipe.\nhypothesis: |\n  Precompute the load/store lane metadata in EX and carry it through the\n  EX/MEM payload so MEM only performs the actual bus access plus a much\n  smaller extract/extend step. This should trim the common memory-path logic\n  without changing retirement semantics or ISA-visible behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add EX/MEM sideband fields for predecoded lane metadata such as alignment, mask, and shift information.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute and latch the memory lane metadata once the effective address is known, instead of re-deriving it in MEM.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-001-r6s0.yaml","time":{"start":1778871625109,"end":1778871625114}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0550eb56f6a52aac016a076d48f4248199b7b2ffeac8cd802a"}},"id":"prt_e2d02e5930010uNet1CYTJMjKK","sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2f76ffeLmDxOQPnceYbHn","messageID":"msg_e2d02d9210012XgQ8fPIShyA7P"}}
