{"type":"text","timestamp":1778871657544,"sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2f76ffeLmDxOQPnceYbHn","part":{"id":"prt_e2d036406001dP13dW9GUMGYFx","messageID":"msg_e2d02f67a001dJYNgg07u8oK4v","sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2f76ffeLmDxOQPnceYbHn","type":"text","text":"I’m writing a bounded two-entry hot-target predictor hypothesis next. It stays in the same “resolved transfer reuse” family as the best prior result, but addresses the one-entry thrash that likely capped it.","time":{"start":1778871657478,"end":1778871657543},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_04b50087e92f3bf4016a076d6955e8819badce26401381ead4","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778871658839,"sessionID":"ses_1d2fe2f76ffeLmDxOQPnceYbHn","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_ho2vbPeYaEFtkp0Dk4HdWDh9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r6s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r6s2\n+title: \"Two-entry hot target cache\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark keeps revisiting the same loop back-edges and a small set of\n+  call/return sites. The prior single-entry hot-target idea shows this class\n+  of predictor can pay off, but one slot can thrash when two hot transfers\n+  alternate. A second bounded entry could raise hit rate without turning IF\n+  into a general BTB or adding branch-immediate decode to the fetch cone.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Expand the hot-transfer predictor into a tiny two-entry cache keyed by the\n+  fetch PC, with both entries trained only from resolved taken control-flow\n+  transfers. Keep fetch-side lookup to two PC compares plus a mux, and keep\n+  training on the existing EX redirect path so no branch-immediate decode or\n+  large history structure enters IF. The extra slot should preserve the loop\n+  back-edge while also remembering a hot call/return site, reducing recurring\n+  wrong-path flushes in CoreMark without materially widening the predictor cone.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add a two-entry hot-target lookup in fetch and choose the predicted next PC from the matching cached transfer.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train or replace the cache from resolved taken branches and JAL/JALR redirects through the existing redirect path.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the resolved transfer metadata between EX and IF without changing the RVFI or memory IO contract.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following fil