{"type":"text","timestamp":1778873907063,"sessionID":"ses_1d2daea10ffeiqBeAUe6rgSRzE","part":{"id":"prt_e2d25b76c001LovGG1zGm3XLsy","messageID":"msg_e2d25a5fd001zaKGTeZcl2o8dv","sessionID":"ses_1d2daea10ffeiqBeAUe6rgSRzE","type":"text","text":"The hypotheses directory isn’t present yet, so I’m creating it with the new hypothesis file in one patch.","time":{"start":1778873907052,"end":1778873907062},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_00f5eba64e6f79cd016a077632a814819987fc7e70c94fc6db","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778873913379,"sessionID":"ses_1d2daea10ffeiqBeAUe6rgSRzE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_No8uajDT5rwyEm4XuwRwC7nr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml\n+id: hyp-20260515-003-r8s2\n+title: \"Two-entry loop predictor\"\n+category: predictor\n+motivation: |\n+  CoreMark is dominated by tight loops, but this core still fetches pc+4 until\n+  EX resolves each branch. A tiny loop-focused predictor can cut repeated\n+  taken-backedge flushes without pulling a general BTB or branch decode into\n+  the IF critical path.\n+hypothesis: |\n+  Add a bounded two-entry loop predictor that only learns from resolved taken\n+  backward B-type branches. IF uses a small PC tag compare plus a predicted\n+  target mux, while EX trains the entry on taken backedges and clears the\n+  confidence on not-taken exits. Limiting the predictor to loop backedges\n+  should capture the hot CoreMark control flow while keeping fetch logic and\n+  formal state small.\n+expected_impact:\n+  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n+  confidence: medium\n+changes:\n+  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Add the two-entry loop predictor lookup and predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"\n+  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n+    description: \"Train the predictor from resolved branch outcomes and redirect on mispredicts.\"\n+  - file: rtl/core.sv\n+    description: \"Thread the predictor update metadata between EX and IF without changing the core IO contract.\"\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-a