{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778873915607,"sessionID":"ses_1d2daea10ffeiqBeAUe6rgSRzE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_A39HMaM75KpKOipwPdrt0AFY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: id: hyp-20260515-003-r8s2\n2: title: \"Two-entry loop predictor\"\n3: category: predictor\n4: motivation: |\n5:   CoreMark is dominated by tight loops, but this core still fetches pc+4 until\n6:   EX resolves each branch. A tiny loop-focused predictor can cut repeated\n7:   taken-backedge flushes without pulling a general BTB or branch decode into\n8:   the IF critical path.\n9: hypothesis: |\n10:   Add a bounded two-entry loop predictor that only learns from resolved taken\n11:   backward B-type branches. IF uses a small PC tag compare plus a predicted\n12:   target mux, while EX trains the entry on taken backedges and clears the\n13:   confidence on not-taken exits. Limiting the predictor to loop backedges\n14:   should capture the hot CoreMark control flow while keeping fetch logic and\n15:   formal state small.\n16: expected_impact:\n17:   fitness_delta_pct: 5\n18:   confidence: medium\n19: changes:\n20:   - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n21:     description: \"Add the two-entry loop predictor lookup and predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"\n22:   - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n23:     description: \"Train the predictor from resolved branch outcomes and redirect on mispredicts.\"\n24:   - file: rtl/core.sv\n25:     description: \"Thread the predictor update metadata between EX and IF without changing the core IO contract.\"\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"id: hyp-20260515-003-r8s2\ntitle: \"Two-entry loop predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  CoreMark is dominated by tight loops, but this core still fetches pc+4 until\n  EX resolves each branch. A tiny loop-focused predictor can cut repeated\n  taken-backedge flushes without pulling a general BTB or branch decode into\n  the IF critical path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a bounded two-entry loop predictor that only learns from resolved taken\n  backward B-type branches. IF uses a small PC tag compare plus a predicted\n  target mux, while EX trains the entry on taken backedges and clears the\n  confidence on not-taken exits. Limiting the predictor to loop backedges\n  should capture the hot CoreMark control flow while keeping fetch logic and\n  formal state small.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20260515-003-r8s2.yaml","time":{"start":1778873915603,"end":1778873915606}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_09b46f88fab105d8016a07763b27fc819986da901f61eec910"}},"id":"prt_e2d25d780002SwPRZkU4ks1kYL","sessionID":"ses_1d2daea10ffeiqBeAUe6rgSRzE","messageID":"msg_e2d25d0b40019lJD1mUvwa4vOg"}}
