{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778875315922,"sessionID":"ses_1d2c52a4cffe4L1kjYjaQmo4b8","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_cqkXLDfGVMhXlVsns7UxJj6N","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl","offset":20,"limit":20},"output":"<path>/Users/bonetto/bonetto/auto-arch-tournament/.claude/bench-runs/gpt-5_4-mini-rep1/cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n20: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Reuse JALR sum\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\\nadder even though the main ALU already produces the same sum for JALR\\ninstructions. That duplicate arithmetic sits in the hot execute cone and\\ncan be shaved without changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\\nadder even though the main ALU already produces the same sum for JALR\\ninstructions. That duplicate arithmetic sits in the hot execute cone and\\ncan be shaved without changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Reuse the main ALU result for JALR redirect generation and factor the\\nrepeated `pc + 4` expression into a shared local so EX does not carry a\\nsecond 32-bit adder for the same instruction. This should trim a small\\namount of combinational depth from the common execute path while keeping\\nthe architectural JAL/JALR results unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the existing ALU sum for JALR target formation and share the pc+4 value across redirect and writeback logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the existing ALU sum for JALR target formation and share the pc+4 value across redirect and writeback logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 262.59, \"delta_pct\": -22.68, \"vs_baseline\": -7.15, \"fmax_mhz\": 117.94, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9949, \"ff\": 1980, \"seeds\": [107.37, 117.94, 127.15], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T19:27:05.990304Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r7s0 (regression, -22.68%): Reusing the ALU sum ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n21: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Split retire snapshot\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB bundle carries both writeback state and a large set of\\nRVFI-only retire fields through the hottest part of the pipeline. That wide\\npayload increases routing and fanout even though most of it is only needed at\\ncommit time.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB bundle carries both writeback state and a large set of\\nRVFI-only retire fields through the hottest part of the pipeline. That wide\\npayload increases routing and fanout even though most of it is only needed at\\ncommit time.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the retirement metadata from the live writeback path: keep a narrow\\nMEM/WB register for regfile writeback and forwarding, and capture the RVFI\\nfields into a separate commit snapshot at the retirement boundary. This should\\nreduce the width and fanout of the common MEM/WB/WB cone while preserving the\\narchitectural stream and all RVFI semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a slimmer live writeback bundle plus a separate retire-snapshot type for RVFI-only metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the narrow writeback state and a separate retirement snapshot instead of carrying one wide shared bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume only the narrow writeback bundle for regfile updates so the fast path no longer drags RVFI fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the retire snapshot to the RVFI outputs while keeping the execution/writeback pipeline semantics unchanged.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a slimmer live writeback bundle plus a separate retire-snapshot type for RVFI-only metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the narr... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n22: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Two-entry return stack\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark and the runtime library spend real time in call/return traffic,\\nbut this core still resolves every JALR return after fetch. A bounded\\nreturn predictor should cut those recurring wrong-path flushes without\\npulling branch-immediate decode or a general BTB into the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark and the runtime library spend real time in call/return traffic,\\nbut this core still resolves every JALR return after fetch. A bounded\\nreturn predictor should cut those recurring wrong-path flushes without\\npulling branch-immediate decode or a general BTB into the IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a tiny two-entry return-address stack that predicts canonical link-\\nregister returns from the fetched opcode/rd/rs1 pattern, and train it only\\nfrom resolved JAL/JALR control flow in EX. Keep B-type branches and non-\\nreturn JALRs on the existing EX-resolved path, so the predictor stays small,\\nformal-friendly, and focused on the call/return behavior CoreMark actually\\nexercises.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a 2-entry return-address stack in fetch and use it to choose the next PC for canonical return-like JALR instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Generate stack push/pop update information from resolved JAL and JALR control flow, and redirect on return mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the predictor update signals between EX and IF without changing the RVFI or memory IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a 2-entry return-address stack in fetch and use it to choose the next PC for canonical return-like JALR instructions.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Gen... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n23: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r8s0\", \"title\": \"Split word-load fast path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is word-load heavy, but the current MEM stage always carries a\\nvariable shift/extract path even when the access is a plain LW. That keeps\\nunnecessary combinational logic on the common retirement path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is word-load heavy, but the current MEM stage always carries a\\nvariable shift/extract path even when the access is a plain LW. That keeps\\nunnecessary combinational logic on the common retirement path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Rework load extraction so the common word-load case takes a direct\\n`dmem_rdata` path, while only byte and halfword loads use the variable\\nshift/extract logic. This should trim the MEM critical cone on the\\nbenchmark's dominant access pattern without changing architectural\\nbehavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the load-data mux so word loads bypass the barrel-shift/extract path and only byte/halfword loads pay for it.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Split the load-data mux so word loads bypass the barrel-shift/extract path and only byte/halfword loads pay for it.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 321.92, \"delta_pct\": -5.21, \"vs_baseline\": 13.83, \"fmax_mhz\": 144.59, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9908, \"ff\": 1960, \"seeds\": [144.59, 157.26, 142.09], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T19:44:47.249384Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r8s0 (regression, -5.21%): Splitting load extraction so `LW` bypasses the shift/extract logic only helps if that variable byte/halfword path is truly on the MEM critical cone; otherwise the added case plu... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n24: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"ID branch resolve\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops, so conditional branch\\nredirects are on a hot path even in a simple in-order core. Moving the\\nB-type compare and redirect decision earlier should shorten the common\\nexecute cone and reduce the cost of taken loop branches.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark spends a lot of time in tight loops, so conditional branch\\nredirects are on a hot path even in a simple in-order core. Moving the\\nB-type compare and redirect decision earlier should shorten the common\\nexecute cone and reduce the cost of taken loop branches.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Resolve B-type branches in ID using the already-decoded branch target and\\nforwarded source operands, while leaving JALR and all non-branch ALU work\\nin EX. This should remove branch compare and redirect selection from the\\nhot EX path without changing architectural results or the load-use stall\\ndiscipline.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a compact branch-resolve sideband so the ID-stage decision can flow through the pipeline cleanly.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/forward_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Retarget operand selection so ID can obtain fresh rs1/rs2 values for conditional branch compares.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare B-type branches in decode, latch the taken decision and redirect target, and emit the early redirect info.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove conditional branch compare work from EX and keep JALR plus ordinary ALU work on the live execute path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Merge the ID-stage branch redirect with the existing control-flow path while preserving the RVFI and memory contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n25: {\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Two-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is dominated by tight loops, but this core still fetches pc+4 until\\nEX resolves each branch. A tiny loop-focused predictor can cut repeated\\ntaken-backedge flushes without pulling a general BTB or branch decode into\\nthe IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is dominated by tight loops, but this core still fetches pc+4 until\\nEX resolves each branch. A tiny loop-focused predictor can cut repeated\\ntaken-backedge flushes without pulling a general BTB or branch decode into\\nthe IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a bounded two-entry loop predictor that only learns from resolved taken\\nbackward B-type branches. IF uses a small PC tag compare plus a predicted\\ntarget mux, while EX trains the entry on taken backedges and clears the\\nconfidence on not-taken exits. Limiting the predictor to loop backedges\\nshould capture the hot CoreMark control flow while keeping fetch logic and\\nformal state small.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the two-entry loop predictor lookup and predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the predictor from resolved branch outcomes and redirect on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the predictor update metadata between EX and IF without changing the core IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the two-entry loop predictor lookup and predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the predictor from resolved branch outcomes and redirect on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the predictor update metadata between EX and IF without changing the core IO contrac... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Reuse JALR sum\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\\nadder even though the main ALU already produces the same sum for JALR\\ninstructions. That duplicate arithmetic sits in the hot execute cone and\\ncan be shaved without changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\