ng the RVFI and memory contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r8s2\", \"title\": \"Two-entry loop predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark is dominated by tight loops, but this core still fetches pc+4 until\\nEX resolves each branch. A tiny loop-focused predictor can cut repeated\\ntaken-backedge flushes without pulling a general BTB or branch decode into\\nthe IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark is dominated by tight loops, but this core still fetches pc+4 until\\nEX resolves each branch. A tiny loop-focused predictor can cut repeated\\ntaken-backedge flushes without pulling a general BTB or branch decode into\\nthe IF critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a bounded two-entry loop predictor that only learns from resolved taken\\nbackward B-type branches. IF uses a small PC tag compare plus a predicted\\ntarget mux, while EX trains the entry on taken backedges and clears the\\nconfidence on not-taken exits. Limiting the predictor to loop backedges\\nshould capture the hot CoreMark control flow while keeping fetch logic and\\nformal state small.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the two-entry loop predictor lookup and predicted-next-PC selection in fetch.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train the predictor from resolved branch outcomes and redirect on mispredicts.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the predictor update metadata between EX and IF without changing the core IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the two-entry loop predict