bus access plus a much\\nsmaller extract/extend step. This should trim the common memory-path logic\\nwithout changing retirement semantics or ISA-visible behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM sideband fields for predecoded lane metadata such as alignment, mask, and shift information.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the memory lane metadata once the effective address is known, instead of re-deriving it in MEM.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried metadata so byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic no longer dominate the MEM cone.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add EX/MEM sideband fields for predecoded lane metadata such as alignment, mask, and shift information.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute and latch the memory lane metadata once the effective address is known, instead of re-deriving it in MEM.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried metadata so byte-mask, alignment, and load-extract logic no longer dominate the MEM cone.\"}], \"outcome\": \"i... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r6s1\", \"title\": \"Dedicated effective-address fast path\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Loads, stores, and JALR all currently route base-plus-offset address formation through the same EX datapath that also serves arithmetic and branch work. On a small FPGA, that shared cone is a natural Fmax limiter, especially in a CoreMark mix with frequent memory traffic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Loads, stores, and JALR all currently route base-plus-offset address formation through the same EX datapath that also serves arithmetic and branch work. On a small FPGA, that shared cone is a natural Fmax limiter, especially in a CoreMark mix with frequent memory traffic.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a dedicated effective-address adder in EX for LOAD, STORE, and JALR, and carry its result as a separate EX/MEM sideband so the main ALU only handles true arithmetic and logic ops. MEM then consumes the sideband directly for address, alignment, and RVFI memory fields. This should shorten the hot execute path without changing architectural retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an EX/MEM sideband field for the dedicated effective-address result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute LOAD/STORE/JALR addresses with a separate adder instead of routing them through the main ALU cone.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the carried effective-address sideband for memory access and RVFI memory reporting.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add an EX/MEM sideband field for the dedicated effective-address result.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compute LOAD/STORE/JALR addresses with a separate adder instead of routing them through the main ALU cone.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume the ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r6s2\", \"title\": \"Two-entry hot target cache\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps revisiting the same loop back-edges and a small set of\\ncall/return sites. The prior single-entry hot-target idea shows this class\\nof predictor can pay off, but one slot can thrash when two hot transfers\\nalternate. A second bounded entry could raise hit rate without turning IF\\ninto a general BTB or adding branch-immediate decode to the fetch cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"CoreMark keeps revisiting the same loop back-edges and a small set of\\ncall/return sites. The prior single-entry hot-target idea shows this class\\nof predictor can pay off, but one slot can thrash when two hot transfers\\nalternate. A second bounded entry could raise hit rate without turning IF\\ninto a general BTB or adding branch-immediate decode to the fetch cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Expand the hot-transfer predictor into a tiny two-entry cache keyed by the\\nfetch PC, with both entries trained only from resolved taken control-flow\\ntransfers. Keep fetch-side lookup to two PC compares plus a mux, and keep\\ntraining on the existing EX redirect path so no branch-immediate decode or\\nlarge history structure enters IF. The extra slot should preserve the loop\\nback-edge while also remembering a hot call/return site, reducing recurring\\nwrong-path flushes in CoreMark without materially widening the predictor cone.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a two-entry hot-target lookup in fetch and choose the predicted next PC from the matching cached transfer.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Train or replace the cache from resolved taken branches and JAL/JALR redirects through the existing redirect path.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Thread the resolved transfer metadata between EX and IF without changing the RVFI or memory IO contract.\"}]}, \"expected_i... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-001-r7s0\", \"title\": \"Reuse JALR sum\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\\nadder even though the main ALU already produces the same sum for JALR\\ninstructions. That duplicate arithmetic sits in the hot execute cone and\\ncan be shaved without changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The EX stage currently computes the JALR target with a separate `rs1 + imm`\\nadder even though the main ALU already produces the same sum for JALR\\ninstructions. That duplicate arithmetic sits in the hot execute cone and\\ncan be shaved without changing retirement behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Reuse the main ALU result for JALR redirect generation and factor the\\nrepeated `pc + 4` expression into a shared local so EX does not carry a\\nsecond 32-bit adder for the same instruction. This should trim a small\\namount of combinational depth from the common execute path while keeping\\nthe architectural JAL/JALR results unchanged.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the existing ALU sum for JALR target formation and share the pc+4 value across redirect and writeback logic.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 3, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Use the existing ALU sum for JALR target formation and share the pc+4 value across redirect and writeback logic.\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 262.59, \"delta_pct\": -22.68, \"vs_baseline\": -7.15, \"fmax_mhz\": 117.94, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 9949, \"ff\": 1980, \"seeds\": [107.37, 117.94, 127.15], \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-15T19:27:05.990304Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-05-15 hyp-20260515-001-r7s0 (regression, -22.68%): Reusing the ALU sum ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-002-r7s1\", \"title\": \"Split retire snapshot\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB bundle carries both writeback state and a large set of\\nRVFI-only retire fields through the hottest part of the pipeline. That wide\\npayload increases routing and fanout even though most of it is only needed at\\ncommit time.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current MEM/WB bundle carries both writeback state and a large set of\\nRVFI-only retire fields through the hottest part of the pipeline. That wide\\npayload increases routing and fanout even though most of it is only needed at\\ncommit time.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Split the retirement metadata from the live writeback path: keep a narrow\\nMEM/WB register for regfile writeback and forwarding, and capture the RVFI\\nfields into a separate commit snapshot at the retirement boundary. This should\\nreduce the width and fanout of the common MEM/WB/WB cone while preserving the\\narchitectural stream and all RVFI semantics.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a slimmer live writeback bundle plus a separate retire-snapshot type for RVFI-only metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the narrow writeback state and a separate retirement snapshot instead of carrying one wide shared bundle.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/wb_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Consume only the narrow writeback bundle for regfile updates so the fast path no longer drags RVFI fields.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Wire the retire snapshot to the RVFI outputs while keeping the execution/writeback pipeline semantics unchanged.\"}]}, \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 4, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Define a slimmer live writeback bundle plus a separate retire-snapshot type for RVFI-only metadata.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Populate the narr... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20260515-003-r7s2\", \"title\": \"Two-entry r